{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZSUV9mUcUsUk5SBoJD1Ko","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing holds without modification. Headline: \"Meta-Brain\n2\t  achieves 78.9% on LIBERO-Plus with ~12M params, outperforming parameter-matched\n3\t  rank-48 universal LoRA by 13.8pp — perturbation-diagnostic routing is a more efficient\n4\t  use of adaptation capacity than uniform correction.\" Ablation ladder strictly monotonic:\n5\t  Frozen (53.6) < Universal-r16 (62.4) < Universal-r48 (65.1) < Random (65.8) < Meta-Brain\n6\t  (78.9) < Oracle (80.7). Existential control (rank-48 universal) cleanly defeated.\n7\t  Random routing offers negligible gain over universal-r48 (+0.7pp, p=0.38, n.s.),\n8\t  ruling out ensemble effects. Oracle gap only 1.8pp, confirming PAR router quality.\n9\t  Clean LIBERO preserved (+0.3pp). Cross-type mismatch drop avg 17.4pp validates expert\n10\t  specialization. Rank sweep shows benefit monotonically increasing (13.8→13.9→14.2pp).\n11\t  All 3 claims stand at full strength. Paper structure: Phase 0 finding → architecture\n12\t  → ablation ladder → per-perturbation cross-type analysis → rank sweep → parameter\n13\t  efficiency. Bibliography covers MoE routing (Switch Transformer, GShard, ST-MoE,\n14\t  V-MoE), VLA robustness (VLA-GSE, SAFE, RobustVLA, FTM, FLA, SRPO, CorridorVLA),\n15\t  LoRA adaptation (LoRA, LoRA-SP, MoIRA, CORAL, AdaLoRA, DoRA), VLA foundations (pi0,\n16\t  OpenVLA, SmolVLA, Octo, RT-2), benchmarks (LIBERO, LIBERO-Plus), reaching 30+ refs\n17\t  comfortably.\n18\t\n19\t  '\n20\timagined_experiments:\n21\t- name: LoRA Expert Training — 3 Specialized + 1 Universal\n22\t  plan_id: plan_002\n23\t  description: 'Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16, Q/K/V/O on all 18 PaliGemma layers,\n24\t    3.7M params each): LoRA-V (online visual augmentation), LoRA-S (oracle spatial\n25\t    demos), LoRA-P (oracle physical demos), Universal (mixed all-perturbation data).\n26\t    Evaluate each expert on its matched type AND cross-type.\n27\t\n28\t    '\n29\t  expected_results:\n30\t    lora_v_on_visual: 80.2\n31\t    lora_v_on_spatial: 62.0\n32\t    lora_v_on_physical: 60.2\n33\t    lora_s_on_visual: 59.5\n34\t    lora_s_on_spatial: 77.5\n35\t    lora_s_on_physical: 60.0\n36\t    lora_p_on_visual: 58.2\n37\t    lora_p_on_spatial: 60.8\n38\t    lora_p_on_physical: 74.8\n39\t    universal_r16_visual: 64.8\n40\t    universal_r16_spatial: 60.5\n41\t    universal_r16_physical: 58.2\n42\t    universal_r16_overall: 62.4\n43\t    cross_type_avg_drop_pp: 17.4\n44\t    val_action_mse_lora_v: 0.0082\n45\t    val_action_mse_lora_s: 0.0091\n46\t    val_action_mse_lora_p: 0.0098\n47\t    val_action_mse_universal: 0.0105\n48\t    convergence_epochs: 15\n49\t  result_rationale: '在 best 档下，perturbation-specific LoRA 学到了质性不同的修正模式。LoRA-V 在 视觉扰动上达到\n50\t    80.2%（+29.4pp over frozen），因为在线增强（camera jitter, brightness shift, background\n51\t    swap, Gaussian noise）精确匹配 LIBERO-Plus 视觉 扰动分布，LoRA 只需学习 early-layer visual representation\n52\t    的低秩修正。LoRA-S 和 LoRA-P 在各自类型上分别达到 77.5%/74.8%，略低于 LoRA-V，原因有二：(1) spatial 和 physical\n53\t    的 oracle demo 采集本身引入采集噪声；(2) 空间和物理扰动涉及 action-level 的高层语义调整，比纯视觉修正的 representation\n54\t    变换更复杂。 关键证据在 cross-type performance：LoRA-V 在 spatial 上仅 62.0%（drop 18.2pp）， 因为视觉修正无法纠正\n55\t    layout 引起的 action trajectory 偏移——这两种修正在 representation space 中方向正交。LoRA-P 在 visual\n56\t    上仅 58.2%（drop 16.6pp）， 因为力学修正作用于 late-layer action planning，反而干扰了本该保持的 early-layer\n57\t    visual features。cross-type 仍高于 frozen（58-62% vs 50-57%），说明 experts 学到了部分可迁移的通用\n58\t    robustness（如 LoRA 的低秩约束本身有 regularization 效果）， 但 type-specific 部分不可互换。Universal\n59\t    LoRA 在各类型上均为中等水平（58-65%）， 是典型的 jack-of-all-trades：3.7M 参数被迫在三种修正方向之间妥协， 每个方向分到的有效容量不足以匹配专有\n60\t    expert。Val MSE 证实了这一点：专有 expert （0.008-0.010）显著低于 universal（0.0105），说明 specialization\n61\t    带来更精确的 action prediction。\n62\t\n63\t    '\n64\t  tables:\n65\t  - name: Cross-type evaluation matrix\n66\t    description: '3×3 expert-vs-type matrix + universal 行。对角线显著高于非对角线 （avg drop 17.4pp），验证修正不可互换。\n67\t\n68\t      '\n69\t    data:\n70\t      headers:\n71\t      - Expert \\ Type\n72\t      - Visual (%)\n73\t      - Spatial (%)\n74\t      - Physical (%)\n75\t      rows:\n76\t      - - LoRA-V\n77\t        - 80.2 ★\n78\t        - '62.0'\n79\t        - '60.2'\n80\t      - - LoRA-S\n81\t        - '59.5'\n82\t        - 77.5 ★\n83\t        - '60.0'\n84\t      - - LoRA-P\n85\t        - '58.2'\n86\t        - '60.8'\n87\t        - 74.8 ★\n88\t      - - Universal-r16\n89\t        - '64.8'\n90\t        - '60.5'\n91\t        - '58.2'\n92\t      - - Frozen pi0\n93\t        - '50.8'\n94\t        - '57.5'\n95\t        - '56.2'\n96\t  figures_description:\n97\t  - Heatmap of cross-type matrix, diagonal cells green, off-diagonal cells orange/red,\n98\t    showing 15-20pp drop\n99\t  - 'Training loss curves: 4 LoRA adapters, showing convergence at ~15 epochs'\n100\t  analysis: 'Cross-type drop 全部 >15pp（最小 15.3pp for LoRA-P on spatial，最大 19.1pp for\n101\t    LoRA-V on spatial/physical avg），直接验证 Claim 2 的前提假设。Universal LoRA 在所有类型上都不如对应的\n102\t    matched expert（差距 12-17pp），确立了 routing 的必要性。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t- name: Meta-Brain Assembly — PAR Router + LoRA Bank E2E\n106\t  plan_id: plan_003\n107\t  description: '组装 PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6, 2-layer MLP, first-token pooling)\n108\t    + 3 LoRA experts，soft routing: h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ_k p(type_k)·LoRA_k(h_frozen)。\n109\t    冻结 LoRA 参数，仅微调 PAR routing weights。全 LIBERO-Plus benchmark 评估。\n110\t\n111\t    '\n112\t  expected_results:\n113\t    libero_plus_overall: 78.9\n114\t    libero_plus_std: 1.2\n115\t    per_type_visual: 81.2\n116\t    per_type_spatial: 77.5\n117\t    per_type_physical: 74.8\n118\t    per_subtype_camera: 78.5\n119\t    per_subtype_light: 83.8\n120\t    per_subtype_background: 80.2\n121\t    per_subtype_noise: 82.1\n122\t    per_subtype_layout: 77.5\n123\t    per_subtype_robot: 74.8\n124\t    routing_weight_visual_on_lora_v: 0.91\n125\t    routing_weight_spatial_on_lora_s: 0.88\n126\t    routing_weight_physical_on_lora_p: 0.86\n127\t    routing_entropy_visual: 0.12\n128\t    routing_entropy_spatial: 0.15\n129\t    routing_entropy_physical: 0.18\n130\t    par_routing_accuracy: 96.8\n131\t    e2e_finetuning_epochs: 5\n132\t    total_trainable_params_M: 11.6\n133\t  result_rationale: '78.9% 整体成功率来自三个因素的协同：(1) PAR router routing accuracy 达 96.8%——\n134\t    Phase 0 已证明 layer 6 first-token 激活在 3-class 上 F1=1.0，端到端微调只需 轻微校准 soft routing\n135\t    的温度参数；(2) soft routing entropy 极低（0.12-0.18）， 说明 router 对每种扰动类型高度确信，routing weights\n136\t    近似 one-hot（视觉扰动时 LoRA-V 权重 0.91），使 Meta-Brain 在运行时近似 oracle routing——这直接解释了 oracle\n137\t    gap 仅 1.8pp；(3) 各 expert 本身质量高（plan_002 验证），routing 只需 选对 expert 即可。per-type 排序\n138\t    V>S>P（81.2>77.5>74.8）反映了扰动修正的内在 难度梯度：视觉扰动是最规则的低秩变换（brightness/contrast 近似线性），空间扰动\n139\t    需要调整 mid-level spatial reasoning，物理扰动涉及 action planning 的高层语义 重构。per-subtype 中\n140\t    light 最高（83.8%）因为亮度变化是最平滑的视觉扰动， camera 稍低（78.5%）因为视角变化需要更复杂的几何 re-projection。Physical\n141\t    expert 的 routing confidence 稍低（0.86 vs 0.91）因为物理扰动在激活空间中的 cluster 略松散（Phase 0:\n142\t    physical F1=0.951 at K=1 vs spatial F1=1.0）。\n143\t\n144\t    '\n145\t  tables:\n146\t  - name: LIBERO-Plus per-perturbation breakdown\n147\t    data:\n148\t      headers:\n149\t      - Perturbation\n150\t      - Type\n151\t      - Success (%)\n152\t      - Δ Frozen (pp)\n153\t      - Routing Weight\n154\t      rows:\n155\t      - - Camera\n156\t        - Visual\n157\t        - '78.5'\n158\t        - '+30.3'\n159\t        - 'LoRA-V: 0.92'\n160\t      - - Light\n161\t        - Visual\n162\t        - '83.8'\n163\t        - '+31.3'\n164\t        - 'LoRA-V: 0.93'\n165\t      - - Background\n166\t        - Visual\n167\t        - '80.2'\n168\t        - '+29.4'\n169\t        - 'LoRA-V: 0.90'\n170\t      - - Noise\n171\t        - Visual\n172\t        - '82.1'\n173\t        - '+28.9'\n174\t        - 'LoRA-V: 0.89'\n175\t      - - Layout\n176\t        - Spatial\n177\t        - '77.5'\n178\t        - '+20.0'\n179\t        - 'LoRA-S: 0.88'\n180\t      - - Robot\n181\t        - Physical\n182\t        - '74.8'\n183\t        - '+18.6'\n184\t        - 'LoRA-P: 0.86'\n185\t      - - Overall\n186\t        - —\n187\t        - '78.9'\n188\t        - '+25.3'\n189\t        - —\n190\t  figures_description:\n191\t  - 'PAR routing weight heatmap 3×3: rows=input perturbation type, cols=LoRA expert,\n192\t    near-diagonal structure'\n193\t  - 'Per-subtype grouped bar chart: Meta-Brain vs Frozen pi0, gain annotated'\n194\t  analysis: '78.9% overall + near-diagonal routing weights + 96.8% routing accuracy\n195\t    共同 构成 best 档核心证据。routing entropy 的 per-type 差异（0.12 visual vs 0.18 physical）反映了\n196\t    Phase 0 分类精度的差异——但即使 physical 的 entropy 也远低于 maximum（0.18 vs log(3)=1.10），确认所有类型的\n197\t    routing 都高度确定。\n198\t\n199\t    '\n200\t- name: Oracle Routing Ablation\n201\t  plan_id: plan_004\n202\t  description: '用 ground-truth 扰动类型标签（hard one-hot）替换 PAR router，测量 learned routing\n203\t    与 perfect routing 的上界差距。\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t  expected_results:\n207\t    oracle_overall: 80.7\n208\t    oracle_std: 0.9\n209\t    oracle_visual: 83.0\n210\t    oracle_spatial: 79.2\n211\t    oracle_physical: 76.5\n212\t    oracle_minus_meta_brain_overall: 1.8\n213\t    oracle_minus_meta_brain_visual: 1.8\n214\t    oracle_minus_meta_brain_spatial: 1.7\n215\t    oracle_minus_meta_brain_physical: 1.7\n216\t  result_rationale: 'Oracle routing 达到 80.7%，仅比 Meta-Brain（78.9%）高 1.8pp。Gap 小于 routing\n217\t    分类错误率所预测的值（routing accuracy 96.8% → 3.2% 错误 → 预期 impact ~3pp）， 因为 PAR 的 soft routing\n218\t    在分类不完全正确时仍分配了较高权重给正确 expert （如 misrouted visual 案例中 LoRA-V 仍获 0.65 权重 vs LoRA-S\n219\t    0.35），使得 routing error 的 downstream impact 被 dampen。per-type gap 高度一致 （1.7-1.8pp），说明\n220\t    PAR router 在三种类型上的性能均衡，没有系统性偏向。 Physical 的 oracle gap（1.7pp）最小，看似反直觉（physical\n221\t    的 routing accuracy 最低），但 physical expert 的 cross-type performance（60.0-60.8%）高于其他\n222\t    expert 的 cross-type（58.2-62.0%），使得 misrouting 的惩罚较轻。\n223\t\n224\t    '\n225\t  tables: []\n226\t  figures_description:\n227\t  - 'Bar chart: Meta-Brain vs Oracle per-type, error bars from 5 seeds, gap annotated'\n228\t  analysis: '1.8pp gap 证明 PAR router 不是系统瓶颈。未来提升应聚焦于 expert 质量 （更好训练数据、更高 rank）而非\n229\t    router 改进。Oracle 结果也为 routing 设定了 performance ceiling：~80.7% 是 rank-16 expert\n230\t    bank 的理论上限。\n231\t\n232\t    '\n233\t- name: Ablation Ladder — Full Systematic Comparison\n234\t  plan_id: plan_005\n235\t  description: 'LIBERO-Plus 上 6 个系统配置的系统对比（5 seeds）：Frozen → Universal-r16 → Universal-r48\n236\t    → Random Routing → Meta-Brain → Oracle。包含 rank-48 parameter-matched control 和\n237\t    random routing baseline。\n238\t\n239\t    '\n240\t  expected_results:\n241\t    frozen_pi0_overall: 53.6\n242\t    frozen_pi0_std: 0.8\n243\t    universal_r16_overall: 62.4\n244\t    universal_r16_std: 1.4\n245\t    universal_r48_overall: 65.1\n246\t    universal_r48_std: 1.3\n247\t    random_routing_overall: 65.8\n248\t    random_routing_std: 2.1\n249\t    meta_brain_overall: 78.9\n250\t    meta_brain_std: 1.2\n251\t    oracle_routing_overall: 80.7\n252\t    oracle_routing_std: 0.9\n253\t    step_frozen_to_r16: 8.8\n254\t    step_r16_to_r48: 2.7\n255\t    step_r48_to_random: 0.7\n256\t    step_random_to_meta_brain: 13.1\n257\t    step_meta_brain_to_oracle: 1.8\n258\t    routing_gap_vs_rank48: 13.8\n259\t    routing_gap_vs_random: 13.1\n260\t    random_vs_r48_pvalue: 0.38\n261\t    meta_brain_vs_random_pvalue: 3.0e-05\n262\t    meta_brain_vs_r48_pvalue: 1.0e-05\n263\t    per_type_visual_frozen: 50.8\n264\t    per_type_spatial_frozen: 57.5\n265\t    per_type_physical_frozen: 56.2\n266\t    per_type_visual_r48: 67.5\n267\t    per_type_spatial_r48: 63.2\n268\t    per_type_physical_r48: 60.8\n269\t    per_type_visual_random: 66.8\n270\t    per_type_spatial_random: 65.5\n271\t    per_type_physical_random: 63.2\n272\t  result_rationale: '消融梯度严格单调递增（53.6→62.4→65.1→65.8→78.9→80.7），每一步对应一个 独立的能力维度： (1)\n273\t    Frozen→r16（+8.8pp）：LoRA 本身提供了通用的 representation correction 能力， 即使不区分扰动类型，低秩修正也能改善\n274\t    feature robustness。 (2) r16→r48（+2.7pp）：增加 rank 有帮助但收益递减——3.2× 参数仅换来 2.7pp， 说明\n275\t    universal correction 的 capacity utilization efficiency 随 rank 下降， 因为额外参数被迫在三种互斥修正方向上妥协。\n276\t    (3) r48→Random（+0.7pp, p=0.38 不显著）：仅 3 个 expert 的 ensemble 效应 几乎不存在。Random routing\n277\t    有时碰巧选对 expert（1/3 概率），拉高了均值， 但也有 2/3 概率选错并导致 suboptimal correction。这两个效应近似抵消，\n278\t    使 random 仅比 universal 高 0.7pp。p=0.38 的不显著性是关键 null result—— 它排除了 \"Meta-Brain 的好处来自\n279\t    ensemble averaging\" 的 alternative explanation。 (4) Random→Meta-Brain（+13.1pp,\n280\t    p<0.001）：整个梯度中最大的单步跳跃。 精确 routing 带来的提升远超 capacity scaling（2.7pp）和 ensemble（0.7pp）的\n281\t    总和——routing 的边际贡献（13.1pp）是 capacity scaling（2.7pp）的 4.9×。 这是 Claim 2 的核心量化证据。\n282\t    (5) Meta-Brain→Oracle（+1.8pp）：PAR router 接近理论上限。 Random routing 的高 std（2.1 vs\n283\t    Meta-Brain 的 1.2）反映了随机 expert 分配的 天然不稳定性——在某些 seed 下碰巧匹配较多，在其他 seed 下则严重不匹配。\n284\t\n285\t    '\n286\t  tables:\n287\t  - name: Ablation Ladder — Main Results (5 seeds)\n288\t    data:\n289\t      headers:\n290\t      - Method\n291\t      - Params\n292\t      - Overall (%)\n293\t      - Visual (%)\n294\t      - Spatial (%)\n295\t      - Physical (%)\n296\t      - Δ Frozen\n297\t      rows:\n298\t      - - Frozen pi0\n299\t        - '0'\n300\t        - 53.6 ± 0.8\n301\t        - '50.8'\n302\t        - '57.5'\n303\t        - '56.2'\n304\t        - —\n305\t      - - Universal r16\n306\t        - 3.7M\n307\t        - 62.4 ± 1.4\n308\t        - '64.8'\n309\t        - '60.5'\n310\t        - '58.2'\n311\t        - '+8.8'\n312\t      - - Universal r48\n313\t        - 12M\n314\t        - 65.1 ± 1.3\n315\t        - '67.5'\n316\t        - '63.2'\n317\t        - '60.8'\n318\t        - '+11.5'\n319\t      - - Random Routing\n320\t        - 12M\n321\t        - 65.8 ± 2.1\n322\t        - '66.8'\n323\t        - '65.5'\n324\t        - '63.2'\n325\t        - '+12.2'\n326\t      - - Meta-Brain (ours)\n327\t        - 12M\n328\t        - 78.9 ± 1.2\n329\t        - '81.2'\n330\t        - '77.5'\n331\t        - '74.8'\n332\t        - '+25.3'\n333\t      - - Oracle Routing\n334\t        - 12M\n335\t        - 80.7 ± 0.9\n336\t        - '83.0'\n337\t        - '79.2'\n338\t        - '76.5'\n339\t        - '+27.1'\n340\t  - name: Statistical significance\n341\t    data:\n342\t      headers:\n343\t      - Comparison\n344\t      - Gap (pp)\n345\t      - p-value\n346\t      - Significant?\n347\t      rows:\n348\t      - - Meta-Brain vs r48\n349\t        - '13.8'\n350\t        - <0.001\n351\t        - Yes (***)\n352\t      - - Meta-Brain vs Random\n353\t        - '13.1'\n354\t        - <0.001\n355\t        - Yes (***)\n356\t      - - Random vs r48\n357\t        - '0.7'\n358\t        - '0.38'\n359\t        - No (n.s.)\n360\t      - - Oracle vs Meta-Brain\n361\t        - '1.8'\n362\t        - '0.03'\n363\t        - Yes (*)\n364\t  figures_description:\n365\t  - 'Bar chart: 6 bars in ablation order, color-coded cold→warm, 5-seed error bars,\n366\t    significance brackets'\n367\t  - 'Decomposition pie chart: routing contribution (13.1pp) vs capacity (2.7pp) vs\n368\t    ensemble (0.7pp) vs baseline (8.8pp)'\n369\t  analysis: '消融梯度提供三个推论：(a) routing >> ensemble（13.1pp vs 0.7pp, ratio 18.7×）； (b)\n370\t    routing >> capacity scaling（13.8pp vs 2.7pp, ratio 5.1×）； (c) PAR ≈ oracle（gap\n371\t    1.8pp）。Random vs r48 的 null result（p=0.38）是 全文最关键的 negative finding——它排除了 Claim\n372\t    2 的唯一 alternative explanation。\n373\t\n374\t    '\n375\t- name: FTM/FLA Reproduction — Visual-Only Baseline\n376\t  plan_id: plan_006\n377\t  description: '在 pi0 backbone 上复现 FTM（Fine-Tuning Masking），对比 FTM vs Meta-Brain 在视觉扰动上的表现，并展示\n378\t    Meta-Brain 在 spatial/physical 上的独特优势。\n379\t\n380\t    '\n381\t  expected_results:\n382\t    ftm_visual_avg: 75.7\n383\t    ftm_camera: 73.2\n384\t    ftm_light: 78.5\n385\t    ftm_background: 74.8\n386\t    ftm_noise: 76.2\n387\t    ftm_spatial: 55.8\n388\t    ftm_physical: 54.5\n389\t    ftm_overall: 65.2\n390\t    ftm_params_K: 4\n391\t    meta_brain_vs_ftm_visual_gap: 5.5\n392\t    meta_brain_vs_ftm_spatial_gap: 21.7\n393\t    meta_brain_vs_ftm_physical_gap: 20.3\n394\t  result_rationale: 'FTM 在 pi0 上复现后视觉扰动达 75.7%（+24.9pp over frozen），以极少参数（4K） 实现了可观修正，验证了\n395\t    FTM 的 feature masking 原理在 pi0 上同样有效—— masking 通过抑制 early-layer 中被扰动 corrupted\n396\t    的 feature channel 来恢复 clean representation。但 FTM 在 spatial（55.8%）和 physical（54.5%）上等同于\n397\t    frozen baseline 甚至略低（spatial -1.7pp），因为 FTM 的核心假设是扰动破坏 视觉特征——对 layout 变化或机器人初始状态变化，masking\n398\t    visual channels 不仅 无益反而可能抑制有用的 spatial/physical 信号。Meta-Brain 在视觉扰动上也高于 FTM（81.2%\n399\t    vs 75.7%，+5.5pp），因为 rank-16 LoRA（3.7M params）比 feature masking（4K params）有更大的修正表达能力——LoRA\n400\t    可以 rotate 和 scale 整个 subspace，而 masking 只能 zero-out channels。但 FTM 的极高参数效率 （4K\n401\t    params for +24.9pp on visual）使其在 visual-only 场景下仍然有独特价值。 核心对比：Meta-Brain 在 spatial/physical\n402\t    上分别高出 FTM 21.7pp 和 20.3pp， 这正是 multi-type routing 的 unique value proposition。\n403\t\n404\t    '\n405\t  tables:\n406\t  - name: FTM vs Meta-Brain comparison\n407\t    data:\n408\t      headers:\n409\t      - Method\n410\t      - Params\n411\t      - Visual (%)\n412\t      - Spatial (%)\n413\t      - Physical (%)\n414\t      - Overall (%)\n415\t      rows:\n416\t      - - Frozen pi0\n417\t        - '0'\n418\t        - '50.8'\n419\t        - '57.5'\n420\t        - '56.2'\n421\t        - '53.6'\n422\t      - - FTM (reprod.)\n423\t        - 4K\n424\t        - '75.7'\n425\t        - '55.8'\n426\t        - '54.5'\n427\t        - '65.2'\n428\t      - - Meta-Brain\n429\t        - 12M\n430\t        - '81.2'\n431\t        - '77.5'\n432\t        - '74.8'\n433\t        - '78.9'\n434\t  figures_description:\n435\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: Visual/Spatial/Physical, 3 bars each (Frozen, FTM, Meta-Brain),\n436\t    showing FTM''s visual-only strength'\n437\t  analysis: 'FTM 是 visual-only robustness 的 strong baseline，且参数效率极高。论文中应定位为 \"single-modality\n438\t    approach 的代表\"——它证明了 visual 修正可以极其高效， 但也证明了 single-modality 无法推广到 multi-type perturbation\n439\t    场景。 Meta-Brain 即使在 visual-only 上也优于 FTM（+5.5pp），说明 LoRA-based correction 比 feature\n440\t    masking 更有表达力。\n441\t\n442\t    '\n443\t- name: Parameter Efficiency Analysis\n444\t  plan_id: plan_007\n445\t  description: '计算各方法的 gain-over-frozen-baseline，按可训练参数归一化， 绘制 parameter efficiency\n446\t    scatter plot。纯分析，无 GPU 计算。\n447\t\n448\t    '\n449\t  expected_results:\n450\t    meta_brain_gain_pp: 25.3\n451\t    meta_brain_params_M: 12\n452\t    meta_brain_gain_per_M: 2.11\n453\t    universal_r16_gain_pp: 8.8\n454\t    universal_r16_params_M: 3.7\n455\t    universal_r16_gain_per_M: 2.38\n456\t    universal_r48_gain_pp: 11.5\n457\t    universal_r48_params_M: 12\n458\t    universal_r48_gain_per_M: 0.96\n459\t    ftm_gain_visual_pp: 24.9\n460\t    ftm_gain_overall_pp: 11.6\n461\t    ftm_params_M: 0.004\n462\t    ftm_gain_per_M_visual: 6225.0\n463\t    ftm_gain_per_M_overall: 2900.0\n464\t    vla_gse_gain_pp: 12.0\n465\t    vla_gse_params_M: 114\n466\t    vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.105\n467\t    meta_brain_pareto_optimal: true\n468\t    meta_brain_vs_r48_efficiency_ratio: 2.2\n469\t  result_rationale: '参数效率分析揭示了三个 regime：(1) 极低参数区（<1M）：FTM 以 4K params 在 visual-only\n470\t    上达到 gain_per_M=6225，但 overall gain_per_M（2900）反映了它 无法覆盖 non-visual 的局限；(2) 中等参数区（1-15M）：Meta-Brain\n471\t    占据 Pareto 前沿——12M params, 25.3pp gain, gain_per_M=2.11。同参数量的 Universal-r48 仅 gain_per_M=0.96，效率差\n472\t    2.2×。这 2.2× 的效率倍数就是 routing 的量化贡献； (3) 高参数区（>100M）：VLA-GSE 的 114M params 仅提供 gain_per_M=0.105\n473\t    （不同 backbone，仅作 suggestive 对比）。即使考虑 backbone 差异，Meta-Brain 的 gain_per_M（2.11）比\n474\t    VLA-GSE（0.105）高 20×，数量级差异足以支撑 parameter efficiency narrative。Universal r16 的 gain_per_M（2.38）看似高于\n475\t    Meta-Brain （2.11），但绝对 gain 仅 8.8pp vs 25.3pp——在 \"达到实用性能阈值\" 的约束下， r16 的高效率无意义，因为\n476\t    62.4% 可能低于部署要求。\n477\t\n478\t    '\n479\t  tables:\n480\t  - name: Parameter efficiency summary\n481\t    data:\n482\t      headers:\n483\t      - Method\n484\t      - Backbone\n485\t      - Params\n486\t      - Gain (pp)\n487\t      - Gain/M\n488\t      - Coverage\n489\t      rows:\n490\t      - - FTM\n491\t        - pi0\n492\t        - 4K\n493\t        - +24.9 (V) / +11.6 (all)\n494\t        - 6225 / 2900\n495\t        - Visual only\n496\t      - - Universal r16\n497\t        - pi0\n498\t        - 3.7M\n499\t        - '+8.8'\n500\t        - '2.38'\n501\t        - All types\n502\t      - - Meta-Brain (ours)\n503\t        - pi0\n504\t        - 12M\n505\t        - '+25.3'\n506\t        - '2.11'\n507\t        - All types\n508\t      - - Universal r48\n509\t        - pi0\n510\t        - 12M\n511\t        - '+11.5'\n512\t        - '0.96'\n513\t        - All types\n514\t      - - VLA-GSE †\n515\t        - Qwen3-4B\n516\t        - 114M\n517\t        - '+12.0'\n518\t        - '0.105'\n519\t        - All types\n520\t  figures_description:\n521\t  - 'Scatter plot: x=trainable params (log scale), y=gain-over-frozen (pp). Meta-Brain\n522\t    on Pareto front. FTM in ultra-low-param corner. VLA-GSE in high-param low-efficiency\n523\t    region (dashed circle, different backbone). Isoquants of gain_per_M as diagonal\n524\t    lines.'\n525\t  analysis: 'Meta-Brain 是 multi-type robustness 场景下的 Pareto optimal 方法。关键 insight：\n526\t    routing 让同等参数预算（12M）的效率提升 2.2×——这不是 architectural overhead 的代价，而是 capacity allocation\n527\t    strategy 的收益。Parameter efficiency scatter 是 Claim 3 的 primary visual evidence。\n528\t\n529\t    '\n530\t- name: Correction Memory Ablation\n531\t  plan_id: plan_008\n532\t  description: '对比 Meta-Brain with/without Correction Memory (CM)，量化 CM 的边际收益。 CM\n533\t    通过 FAISS 检索相似历史扰动的 routing weight 来调制当前 routing。\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t  expected_results:\n537\t    meta_brain_no_cm: 78.9\n538\t    meta_brain_with_cm: 80.1\n539\t    cm_delta_overall: 1.2\n540\t    cm_delta_visual: 0.8\n541\t    cm_delta_spatial: 1.5\n542\t    cm_delta_physical: 1.8\n543\t    cm_additional_params: 1\n544\t    cm_latency_overhead_ms: 2.3\n545\t    cm_pvalue: 0.08\n546\t  result_rationale: 'CM 提供 +1.2pp 整体提升（p=0.08, borderline significant with 5 seeds），\n547\t    主要来自 spatial（+1.5pp）和 physical（+1.8pp）而非 visual（+0.8pp）。 这符合 CM 的设计逻辑：CM 检索与当前\n548\t    observation 最相似的历史扰动 exemplar， 用其 routing weight 作为 contextual prior 来调制 PAR 输出。Spatial\n549\t    和 physical 扰动的 within-type 变异更大（不同 layout randomization 的具体形态差异远大于 不同 lighting\n550\t    condition），历史 exemplar 能提供有用的 \"这种具体 layout 变化 应该如何调整 routing\" 的信息。Visual 上 CM\n551\t    收益小因为 PAR 对视觉扰动已经 足够准确（routing accuracy ~98% on visual），contextual modulation\n552\t    的改进空间 有限。但 +1.2pp 的总收益与 1 个额外可学习参数 + 2.3ms CPU latency 相比， cost-benefit 偏低——不值得作为\n553\t    named architectural component 推广。\n554\t\n555\t    '\n556\t  tables: []\n557\t  figures_description:\n558\t  - 'Ablation bar chart: with/without CM, per-type Δ annotated, p-value shown'\n559\t  analysis: 'CM 是 optional module，+1.2pp 不改变任何 claim 的结论。论文呈现策略： 一行 ablation 文字 +\n560\t    footnote table，明确标注 \"optional, borderline significant\"。 Dream reviewers 一致认为 CM\n561\t    是 padding，降级处理是正确决策。\n562\t\n563\t    '\n564\t- name: Router Architecture Comparison\n565\t  plan_id: plan_009\n566\t  description: '对比 3 种 PAR router 变体：2-layer MLP (default), linear classifier, attention-based\n567\t    router。均使用 PaliGemma layer 6 first-token features。\n568\t\n569\t    '\n570\t  expected_results:\n571\t    mlp_routing_accuracy: 96.8\n572\t    mlp_downstream: 78.9\n573\t    mlp_params_M: 0.53\n574\t    linear_routing_accuracy: 94.2\n575\t    linear_downstream: 76.8\n576\t    linear_params_M: 0.01\n577\t    attention_routing_accuracy: 97.1\n578\t    attention_downstream: 78.5\n579\t    attention_params_M: 1.85\n580\t  result_rationale: 'MLP（96.8% routing, 78.9% downstream）是最优 cost-performance 均衡。Linear\n581\t    分类器准确率低 2.6pp（94.2%），因为 3-class 边界在激活空间中有轻微非线性—— Phase 0 t-SNE 显示 Spatial/Physical\n582\t    cluster 的边界不完全线性可分（两者都 影响 action space，共享部分特征），MLP 的一层隐藏层足以 model 这个非线性。 2.6pp\n583\t    routing gap 转化为 2.1pp downstream gap（76.8% vs 78.9%），说明 routing accuracy 和 task\n584\t    success 近似线性相关但有 damping（soft routing 缓冲了部分 routing error）。Attention-based router\n585\t    routing accuracy 最高 （97.1%），但 downstream 反而略低（78.5%），因为 1.85M 额外参数在仅 5 epoch 微调下轻微\n586\t    overfit——attention 的表达能力对 3-class routing 过剩。\n587\t\n588\t    '\n589\t  tables:\n590\t  - name: Router architecture comparison\n591\t    data:\n592\t      headers:\n593\t      - Router Type\n594\t      - Params (M)\n595\t      - Routing Acc (%)\n596\t      - Downstream (%)\n597\t      rows:\n598\t      - - Linear\n599\t        - '0.01'\n600\t        - '94.2'\n601\t        - '76.8'\n602\t      - - 2-layer MLP ★\n603\t        - '0.53'\n604\t        - '96.8'\n605\t        - '78.9'\n606\t      - - Attention\n607\t        - '1.85'\n608\t        - '97.1'\n609\t        - '78.5'\n610\t  figures_description: []\n611\t  analysis: 'Router 架构的 downstream impact 有限（max spread 2.1pp），说明 Meta-Brain 的性能主要由\n612\t    routing 原理和 expert 质量驱动，而非 router 实现细节。 论文中作简短 ablation paragraph 处理。\n613\t\n614\t    '\n615\t- name: 6-class vs 3-class Routing\n616\t  plan_id: plan_010\n617\t  description: '对比 6-class 精细路由（camera/light/background/noise/layout/robot 各一个 LoRA\n618\t    expert，6×3.7M=22.1M params）vs 3-class 粗路由（Visual/Spatial/Physical， 3×3.7M=11.1M\n619\t    params）。\n620\t\n621\t    '\n622\t  expected_results:\n623\t    3class_overall: 78.9\n624\t    3class_params_M: 12\n625\t    6class_overall: 79.6\n626\t    6class_params_M: 24\n627\t    6class_delta: 0.7\n628\t    6class_camera: 80.2\n629\t    6class_light: 84.5\n630\t    6class_background: 81.0\n631\t    6class_noise: 83.2\n632\t    6class_layout: 77.8\n633\t    6class_robot: 75.1\n634\t    marginal_gain_per_expert: 0.23\n635\t    6class_routing_accuracy: 94.8\n636\t  result_rationale: '6-class 仅比 3-class 高 0.7pp（79.6% vs 78.9%），参数量翻倍（24M vs 12M），\n637\t    每额外 expert 的边际收益仅 0.23pp。这与 Phase 0 的发现一致：intra-Visual 4 个 sub-type 在激活空间中形成一个紧致\n638\t    cluster（6-class accuracy 99.8% 但 sub-type 间 cosine similarity 高达 0.92），说明 camera/light/background/noise\n639\t    的修正策略高度重叠——它们都影响 early-layer visual representation，差异更多是 程度而非类型。Independent camera\n640\t    expert 比 shared LoRA-V 仅高 1.7pp（80.2% vs 78.5%），代价是独占 3.7M 参数。同时 6-class routing\n641\t    accuracy 下降到 94.8% （vs 3-class 96.8%），因为 6-class 边界更精细，分类更困难，少量 routing error\n642\t    部分抵消了 expert specialization 的收益。3-class 是 granularity 的 sweet spot。\n643\t\n644\t    '\n645\t  tables:\n646\t  - name: Granularity comparison\n647\t    data:\n648\t      headers:\n649\t      - Granularity\n650\t      - Experts\n651\t      - Total Params\n652\t      - Overall (%)\n653\t      - Routing Acc (%)\n654\t      - Δ\n655\t      rows:\n656\t      - - 3-class\n657\t        - '3'\n658\t        - 12M\n659\t        - '78.9'\n660\t        - '96.8'\n661\t        - —\n662\t      - - 6-class\n663\t        - '6'\n664\t        - 24M\n665\t        - '79.6'\n666\t        - '94.8'\n667\t        - '+0.7'\n668\t  figures_description: []\n669\t  analysis: '0.7pp / 2× params 的 trade-off 验证了 3-class taxonomy 的合理性，回应 Reviewer C5。Phase\n670\t    0 的 Visual cluster 紧致性是根本原因——finer granularity within Visual 增加 routing 难度但不增加修正多样性。\n671\t\n672\t    '\n673\t- name: Rank-48 Parameter-Matched Universal LoRA — Existential Control\n674\t  plan_id: plan_013\n675\t  description: '训练 rank-48 universal LoRA（~11.1M params，精确匹配 Meta-Brain 的 3×rank-16\n676\t    expert 参数总量）。若 rank-48 ≈ Meta-Brain → Claim 2 崩溃。\n677\t\n678\t    '\n679\t  expected_results:\n680\t    rank48_overall: 65.1\n681\t    rank48_std: 1.3\n682\t    rank48_visual: 67.5\n683\t    rank48_spatial: 63.2\n684\t    rank48_physical: 60.8\n685\t    rank48_vs_meta_brain_gap: 13.8\n686\t    rank48_vs_r16_improvement: 2.7\n687\t    rank48_gain_over_frozen: 11.5\n688\t    rank48_gain_per_M: 0.96\n689\t    claim2_survival: true\n690\t  result_rationale: 'Rank-48 universal LoRA 达到 65.1%（+11.5pp over frozen），仅比 rank-16\n691\t    （62.4%）高 2.7pp，despite 3.2× 参数增长（3.7M → 11.1M）。这证实了 \"universal capacity saturation\"\n692\t    假设：uniform LoRA 的收益在 rank 16-48 之间快速递减。根本原因：rank-48 的 11.1M 参数被迫在三种修正方向（visual:\n693\t    early-layer re-projection, spatial: mid-layer trajectory adjustment, physical:\n694\t    late-layer action re-planning）之间共享。这三种修正在 representation space 中 方向不同甚至互斥——改善\n695\t    visual robustness 的 rank 方向可能削弱 spatial 性能。 增加 rank 只是增加了妥协的参数量，无法解决方向冲突。per-type\n696\t    分布清晰展示了 这个困境：Visual（67.5%）的 gain over frozen（+16.7pp）远大于 Spatial（+5.7pp） 和 Physical（+4.6pp），因为\n697\t    visual perturbation 在混合训练数据中占 4/6 sub-types， universal LoRA 被 biased toward visual\n698\t    correction。Meta-Brain 的 3 experts 各自专注一种类型，消除了方向冲突和数据 imbalance。13.8pp gap（p<0.001）\n699\t    是 Claim 2 的 existential validation：identical parameter budget, dramatically different\n700\t    outcome。\n701\t\n702\t    '\n703\t  tables: []\n704\t  figures_description:\n705\t  - 'Embedded in ablation ladder figure: rank-48 bar annotated with ''= Meta-Brain\n706\t    params'' and 13.8pp gap arrow'\n707\t  analysis: '全文最关键的单个实验。13.8pp gap + p<0.001 直接证明 routing 的价值不可被 parameter scaling\n708\t    替代。如果这个 gap <5pp，整篇论文的 thesis 就需要根本性重构。 在 best 档下，gap 足够大且稳健，Claim 2 完整存活。\n709\t\n710\t    '\n711\t- name: LoRA Rank Sweep (r=16/32/64)\n712\t  plan_id: plan_014\n713\t  description: '在 r=16/32/64 三个 expert rank 上分别训练 Meta-Brain 和 parameter-matched universal\n714\t    LoRA，测试 routing benefit 是否随 expert capacity 增长而变化。\n715\t\n716\t    '\n717\t  expected_results:\n718\t    r16_meta_brain: 78.9\n719\t    r16_universal_matched: 65.1\n720\t    r16_routing_benefit: 13.8\n721\t    r16_total_params_M: 12\n722\t    r32_meta_brain: 81.5\n723\t    r32_universal_matched: 67.6\n724\t    r32_routing_benefit: 13.9\n725\t    r32_total_params_M: 24\n726\t    r64_meta_brain: 84.2\n727\t    r64_universal_matched: 70.0\n728\t    r64_routing_benefit: 14.2\n729\t    r64_total_params_M: 48\n730\t    benefit_trend: monotonically increasing\n731\t    universal_diminishing_returns_r48_to_r96: 2.5\n732\t    universal_diminishing_returns_r96_to_r192: 2.4\n733\t  result_rationale: 'Routing benefit 单调递增（13.8→13.9→14.2pp），排除了 Dream worst-case \"routing\n734\t    benefit 仅在特定 capacity 下出现\" 的顾虑。递增的机制： (1) 更高 rank 的 expert 能捕获更精细的 type-specific\n735\t    correction（r=64 LoRA-V on visual ~86%），这些精细修正的价值在 universal setting 下被 dilute\n736\t    掉—— universal 必须在三种修正之间分配每一个 rank component。 (2) Universal LoRA 的 scaling 呈递减：r48→r96\n737\t    仅 +2.5pp, r96→r192 仅 +2.4pp， 因为额外 rank 被用于 refine 已有的妥协方案，而非学习新的修正维度。 (3) Meta-Brain\n738\t    的 scaling 近似线性（78.9→81.5→84.2，每次 ~+2.6pp）， 因为每个 expert 的额外 rank 直接用于 deepen 该类型的专有修正，没有\n739\t    cross-type interference。两条 scaling curve 的斜率差导致 benefit gap 缓慢扩大。 这个 finding 的叙事意义：routing\n740\t    benefit 不是特定 capacity 的 artifact， 而是 fundamental architectural advantage——无论参数预算大小，routing\n741\t    始终优于 uniform correction。如果有更多参数预算，应投入到更高 rank 的 routed experts。\n742\t\n743\t    '\n744\t  tables:\n745\t  - name: Rank sweep results\n746\t    data:\n747\t      headers:\n748\t      - Expert Rank\n749\t      - Meta-Brain (%)\n750\t      - Matched Universal (%)\n751\t      - Routing Benefit (pp)\n752\t      - Total Params\n753\t      rows:\n754\t      - - r=16\n755\t        - '78.9'\n756\t        - '65.1'\n757\t        - '13.8'\n758\t        - 12M\n759\t      - - r=32\n760\t        - '81.5'\n761\t        - '67.6'\n762\t        - '13.9'\n763\t        - 24M\n764\t      - - r=64\n765\t        - '84.2'\n766\t        - '70.0'\n767\t        - '14.2'\n768\t        - 48M\n769\t  figures_description:\n770\t  - 'Line plot: x=rank (log scale), y=success rate. Two lines (Meta-Brain, Universal),\n771\t    diverging gap annotated at each rank'\n772\t  analysis: 'Monotonically increasing routing benefit 是一个 clean scaling result。 它也暗示\n773\t    r=64 Meta-Brain（84.2%）可以 match 或超过 VLA-GSE（81.2%，不同 backbone），虽然 cross-backbone\n774\t    对比是 indirect，但趋势线的 extrapolation 支持 Meta-Brain 在更高 capacity 下的 competitive potential。\n775\t\n776\t    '\n777\t- name: Clean LIBERO Evaluation\n778\t  plan_id: plan_015\n779\t  description: '在标准（无扰动）LIBERO 上评估 Meta-Brain 和 baselines，验证 routing 不会 降低 nominal\n780\t    performance。\n781\t\n782\t    '\n783\t  expected_results:\n784\t    frozen_pi0_clean: 91.2\n785\t    universal_r16_clean: 90.8\n786\t    universal_r48_clean: 90.5\n787\t    meta_brain_clean: 91.5\n788\t    clean_delta_meta_brain: 0.3\n789\t    clean_delta_r16: -0.4\n790\t    clean_delta_r48: -0.7\n791\t    par_routing_entropy_on_clean: 0.85\n792\t    par_routing_weight_distribution_clean: ≈ 0.34/0.33/0.33\n793\t  result_rationale: 'Meta-Brain 在 clean LIBERO 上 91.5%（Δ=+0.3pp vs frozen），完全保持 nominal\n794\t    性能。这得益于 PAR router 的一个 emergent 行为：在无扰动输入下，layer 6 first-token 激活不匹配任何已知扰动 pattern，PAR\n795\t    输出高 entropy（0.85， 接近 max log(3)=1.10），routing weights 近似均匀（~0.33/0.33/0.33）。 三个\n796\t    expert 的修正在 clean input 上大致方向相反（各自 tuned 为不同扰动的 correction），均匀加权后 net correction\n797\t    ≈ 0——routing 自动 degrade to identity。微弱的 +0.3pp 正 delta 可能来自 expert LoRA 的轻微 regularization\n798\t    效果。对比 Universal LoRA：r16 下降 0.4pp, r48 下降 0.7pp，因为 universal LoRA 始终应用 correction（无\n799\t    \"关闭\" 机制），对 clean input 造成不必要的 representation perturbation。Rank 越高干扰越大（r48 的 -0.7pp），因为\n800\t    higher-rank LoRA 的 representation 修改幅度更大。这为 deployment 增加了 重要论据：Meta-Brain 的 routing\n801\t    机制在正常条件下安全 graceful degrade， 而 always-on universal correction 有代价。\n802\t\n803\t    '\n804\t  tables:\n805\t  - name: Clean LIBERO preservation\n806\t    data:\n807\t      headers:\n808\t      - Method\n809\t      - Clean LIBERO (%)\n810\t      - Δ vs Frozen (pp)\n811\t      rows:\n812\t      - - Frozen pi0\n813\t        - '91.2'\n814\t        - —\n815\t      - - Universal r16\n816\t        - '90.8'\n817\t        - '-0.4'\n818\t      - - Universal r48\n819\t        - '90.5'\n820\t        - '-0.7'\n821\t      - - Meta-Brain\n822\t        - '91.5'\n823\t        - '+0.3'\n824\t  figures_description: []\n825\t  analysis: 'Clean LIBERO preservation 是 practical deployment argument 的关键证据。 Meta-Brain\n826\t    是唯一在 perturbed 和 clean 条件下都不降级的方法。PAR routing 的 high-entropy fallback 是一个 emergent\n827\t    property（非刻意设计），可作为 \"routing 自动 detect perturbation absence\" 的附加 insight 呈现。\n828\t\n829\t    '\n830\t- name: Cross-Backbone Validation (SmolVLA)\n831\t  plan_id: plan_011\n832\t  description: '在 SmolVLA 上复现 Phase 0 + Phase 1 核心 pipeline，验证 perturbation-diagnostic\n833\t    routing 的跨架构泛化性。P2 优先级。\n834\t\n835\t    '\n836\t  expected_results:\n837\t    smolvla_phase0_3class_f1: 0.971\n838\t    smolvla_phase0_best_layer: 4\n839\t    smolvla_frozen_libero_plus: 49.8\n840\t    smolvla_universal_r16: 58.2\n841\t    smolvla_meta_brain: 72.4\n842\t    smolvla_gain_over_frozen: 22.6\n843\t    smolvla_routing_benefit_vs_universal: 14.2\n844\t    smolvla_routing_accuracy: 94.5\n845\t  result_rationale: 'SmolVLA Phase 0 F1=0.971（vs pi0 0.993），略低但仍极高，验证了 perturbation\n846\t    diagnosability 不是 PaliGemma 架构的特有属性。Best layer 是 layer 4 （SmolVLA 共 ~12 层），深度比例\n847\t    ~1/3 与 pi0 的 layer 6/18 一致， 暗示 perturbation information 在 VLA 中的 consolidation\n848\t    发生在相对一致的 depth fraction。Phase 0 F1 略低的原因：SmolVLA 的 representation 维度更小， perturbation\n849\t    cluster 间的 margin 更窄，但仍足以支撑高质量 routing。 Meta-Brain on SmolVLA 达到 72.4%（+22.6pp\n850\t    over frozen 49.8%）， routing benefit vs universal 为 14.2pp（vs pi0 上的 13.8pp），定量吻合度很高。\n851\t    SmolVLA 绝对性能低于 pi0（72.4% vs 78.9%）因为 backbone capacity 更小， 但 routing benefit 的相对大小几乎相同（14.2\n852\t    vs 13.8），说明 routing 的价值不依赖于 backbone quality——无论 backbone 强弱， perturbation-type-specific\n853\t    correction 都比 uniform correction 更高效。\n854\t\n855\t    '\n856\t  tables:\n857\t  - name: Cross-backbone comparison\n858\t    data:\n859\t      headers:\n860\t      - Metric\n861\t      - pi0 (PaliGemma)\n862\t      - SmolVLA\n863\t      rows:\n864\t      - - Phase 0 3-class F1\n865\t        - '0.993'\n866\t        - '0.971'\n867\t      - - Best probing layer\n868\t        - 6 / 18\n869\t        - 4 / 12\n870\t      - - Frozen baseline (%)\n871\t        - '53.6'\n872\t        - '49.8'\n873\t      - - Universal r16 (%)\n874\t        - '62.4'\n875\t        - '58.2'\n876\t      - - Meta-Brain (%)\n877\t        - '78.9'\n878\t        - '72.4'\n879\t      - - Routing benefit (pp)\n880\t        - '13.8'\n881\t        - '14.2'\n882\t  figures_description:\n883\t  - 'Paired bar chart: pi0 vs SmolVLA, routing benefit annotated, showing consistency'\n884\t  analysis: 'Cross-backbone validation 将 contribution 从 \"pi0 上有效的 technique\" 提升为 \"VLA\n885\t    的通用 robustness principle\"。routing benefit 在两个 backbone 上的 高度一致性（13.8 vs 14.2pp）是最有说服力的\n886\t    generalization evidence。 直接回应 Reviewer C3。\n887\t\n888\t    '\n889\t- name: LoRA Layer Placement Ablation\n890\t  plan_id: plan_012\n891\t  description: '对比不同 PaliGemma 层覆盖范围（early 2-6, mid 6-12, late 12-16, all 2-16） 对各\n892\t    expert type 的影响。P2 优先级。\n893\t\n894\t    '\n895\t  expected_results:\n896\t    lora_v_early: 78.5\n897\t    lora_v_mid: 76.2\n898\t    lora_v_late: 72.8\n899\t    lora_v_all: 80.2\n900\t    lora_s_early: 73.5\n901\t    lora_s_mid: 76.8\n902\t    lora_s_late: 74.2\n903\t    lora_s_all: 77.5\n904\t    lora_p_early: 69.8\n905\t    lora_p_mid: 72.5\n906\t    lora_p_late: 74.5\n907\t    lora_p_all: 74.8\n908\t    v_best_subset: early (2-6)\n909\t    s_best_subset: mid (6-12)\n910\t    p_best_subset: late (12-16)\n911\t    v_all_minus_best_subset: 1.7\n912\t    s_all_minus_best_subset: 0.7\n913\t    p_all_minus_best_subset: 0.3\n914\t  result_rationale: 'Layer placement 揭示了清晰的 V→early, S→mid, P→late 偏好梯度： LoRA-V 在\n915\t    early layers 最优 subset（78.5%），因为视觉扰动（camera/light/ background/noise）破坏 early visual\n916\t    representation——在损坏发生处修正最高效。 Late layers（72.8%）最差（-7.4pp vs all），因为 corrupted\n917\t    features 已经 propagate 到深层并 compound，late-layer 修正无法 undo upstream corruption。\n918\t    LoRA-S 在 mid layers 最优（76.8%），因为 spatial perturbation（layout 变化） 影响的是 visual-to-spatial\n919\t    reasoning 的转换阶段——mid layers 将 2D visual features 转化为 3D spatial-action representations。LoRA-P\n920\t    在 late layers 最优（74.5%），且与 all-layer（74.8%）仅差 0.3pp，因为 physical perturbation （robot\n921\t    初始状态变化）影响 high-level action planning，这发生在 late decision layers。但所有 expert 在 all-layer\n922\t    覆盖下均为最优或接近最优，说明 cross-layer redundancy 有益——即使存在层偏好，拥有 all-layer coverage 可以 catch\n923\t    residual perturbation effects at other layers。v_all_minus_best_subset 最大（1.7pp），\n924\t    说明 visual perturbation 虽集中在 early layers 但 mid/late 仍有 residual impact。\n925\t\n926\t    '\n927\t  tables:\n928\t  - name: Layer placement ablation\n929\t    data:\n930\t      headers:\n931\t      - Layers\n932\t      - LoRA-V Visual (%)\n933\t      - LoRA-S Spatial (%)\n934\t      - LoRA-P Physical (%)\n935\t      rows:\n936\t      - - Early (2-6)\n937\t        - 78.5 ★V\n938\t        - '73.5'\n939\t        - '69.8'\n940\t      - - Mid (6-12)\n941\t        - '76.2'\n942\t        - 76.8 ★S\n943\t        - '72.5'\n944\t      - - Late (12-16)\n945\t        - '72.8'\n946\t        - '74.2'\n947\t        - 74.5 ★P\n948\t      - - All (2-16)\n949\t        - '80.2'\n950\t        - '77.5'\n951\t        - '74.8'\n952\t  figures_description:\n953\t  - '3×4 heatmap: rows=layer range, cols=expert type, ★=best subset per expert, diagonal\n954\t    pattern visible'\n955\t  analysis: V→early, S→mid, P→late 的对应关系提供了 mechanistic insight，支撑 \"不同扰动 影响不同处理阶段\"\n956\t    的理论框架。这个 finding 虽然不影响主要 claim（all-layer 仍是实用最优），但作为 practical insight 增加了论文的理论深度。未来工作可\n957\t    探索 layer-specific routing（根据扰动类型动态选择 active layers）。\n958\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d09a97eb-2874-493a-b7bd-2546bcb68a45","uuid":"f7a0f75e-6dcd-4ad3-9b73-f476cea50e1d","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:09:28.791Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/meta_brain_lora_routing/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T165902/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Original framing holds without modification. Headline: \"Meta-Brain\n  achieves 78.9% on LIBERO-Plus with ~12M params, outperforming parameter-matched\n  rank-48 universal LoRA by 13.8pp — perturbation-diagnostic routing is a more efficient\n  use of adaptation capacity than uniform correction.\" Ablation ladder strictly monotonic:\n  Frozen (53.6) < Universal-r16 (62.4) < Universal-r48 (65.1) < Random (65.8) < Meta-Brain\n  (78.9) < Oracle (80.7). Existential control (rank-48 universal) cleanly defeated.\n  Random routing offers negligible gain over universal-r48 (+0.7pp, p=0.38, n.s.),\n  ruling out ensemble effects. Oracle gap only 1.8pp, confirming PAR router quality.\n  Clean LIBERO preserved (+0.3pp). Cross-type mismatch drop avg 17.4pp validates expert\n  specialization. Rank sweep shows benefit monotonically increasing (13.8→13.9→14.2pp).\n  All 3 claims stand at full strength. Paper structure: Phase 0 finding → architecture\n  → ablation ladder → per-perturbation cross-type analysis → rank sweep → parameter\n  efficiency. Bibliography covers MoE routing (Switch Transformer, GShard, ST-MoE,\n  V-MoE), VLA robustness (VLA-GSE, SAFE, RobustVLA, FTM, FLA, SRPO, CorridorVLA),\n  LoRA adaptation (LoRA, LoRA-SP, MoIRA, CORAL, AdaLoRA, DoRA), VLA foundations (pi0,\n  OpenVLA, SmolVLA, Octo, RT-2), benchmarks (LIBERO, LIBERO-Plus), reaching 30+ refs\n  comfortably.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: LoRA Expert Training — 3 Specialized + 1 Universal\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16, Q/K/V/O on all 18 PaliGemma layers,\n    3.7M params each): LoRA-V (online visual augmentation), LoRA-S (oracle spatial\n    demos), LoRA-P (oracle physical demos), Universal (mixed all-perturbation data).\n    Evaluate each expert on its matched type AND cross-type.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    lora_v_on_visual: 80.2\n    lora_v_on_spatial: 62.0\n    lora_v_on_physical: 60.2\n    lora_s_on_visual: 59.5\n    lora_s_on_spatial: 77.5\n    lora_s_on_physical: 60.0\n    lora_p_on_visual: 58.2\n    lora_p_on_spatial: 60.8\n    lora_p_on_physical: 74.8\n    universal_r16_visual: 64.8\n    universal_r16_spatial: 60.5\n    universal_r16_physical: 58.2\n    universal_r16_overall: 62.4\n    cross_type_avg_drop_pp: 17.4\n    val_action_mse_lora_v: 0.0082\n    val_action_mse_lora_s: 0.0091\n    val_action_mse_lora_p: 0.0098\n    val_action_mse_universal: 0.0105\n    convergence_epochs: 15\n  result_rationale: '在 best 档下，perturbation-specific LoRA 学到了质性不同的修正模式。LoRA-V 在 视觉扰动上达到\n    80.2%（+29.4pp over frozen），因为在线增强（camera jitter, brightness shift, background\n    swap, Gaussian noise）精确匹配 LIBERO-Plus 视觉 扰动分布，LoRA 只需学习 early-layer visual representation\n    的低秩修正。LoRA-S 和 LoRA-P 在各自类型上分别达到 77.5%/74.8%，略低于 LoRA-V，原因有二：(1) spatial 和 physical\n    的 oracle demo 采集本身引入采集噪声；(2) 空间和物理扰动涉及 action-level 的高层语义调整，比纯视觉修正的 representation\n    变换更复杂。 关键证据在 cross-type performance：LoRA-V 在 spatial 上仅 62.0%（drop 18.2pp）， 因为视觉修正无法纠正\n    layout 引起的 action trajectory 偏移——这两种修正在 representation space 中方向正交。LoRA-P 在 visual\n    上仅 58.2%（drop 16.6pp）， 因为力学修正作用于 late-layer action planning，反而干扰了本该保持的 early-layer\n    visual features。cross-type 仍高于 frozen（58-62% vs 50-57%），说明 experts 学到了部分可迁移的通用\n    robustness（如 LoRA 的低秩约束本身有 regularization 效果）， 但 type-specific 部分不可互换。Universal\n    LoRA 在各类型上均为中等水平（58-65%）， 是典型的 jack-of-all-trades：3.7M 参数被迫在三种修正方向之间妥协， 每个方向分到的有效容量不足以匹配专有\n    expert。Val MSE 证实了这一点：专有 expert （0.008-0.010）显著低于 universal（0.0105），说明 specialization\n    带来更精确的 action prediction。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-type evaluation matrix\n    description: '3×3 expert-vs-type matrix + universal 行。对角线显著高于非对角线 （avg drop 17.4pp），验证修正不可互换。\n\n      '\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Expert \\ Type\n      - Visual (%)\n      - Spatial (%)\n      - Physical (%)\n      rows:\n      - - LoRA-V\n        - 80.2 ★\n        - '62.0'\n        - '60.2'\n      - - LoRA-S\n        - '59.5'\n        - 77.5 ★\n        - '60.0'\n      - - LoRA-P\n        - '58.2'\n        - '60.8'\n        - 74.8 ★\n      - - Universal-r16\n        - '64.8'\n        - '60.5'\n        - '58.2'\n      - - Frozen pi0\n        - '50.8'\n        - '57.5'\n        - '56.2'\n  figures_description:\n  - Heatmap of cross-type matrix, diagonal cells green, off-diagonal cells orange/red,\n    showing 15-20pp drop\n  - 'Training loss curves: 4 LoRA adapters, showing convergence at ~15 epochs'\n  analysis: 'Cross-type drop 全部 >15pp（最小 15.3pp for LoRA-P on spatial，最大 19.1pp for\n    LoRA-V on spatial/physical avg），直接验证 Claim 2 的前提假设。Universal LoRA 在所有类型上都不如对应的\n    matched expert（差距 12-17pp），确立了 routing 的必要性。\n\n    '\n- name: Meta-Brain Assembly — PAR Router + LoRA Bank E2E\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '组装 PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6, 2-layer MLP, first-token pooling)\n    + 3 LoRA experts，soft routing: h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ_k p(type_k)·LoRA_k(h_frozen)。\n    冻结 LoRA 参数，仅微调 PAR routing weights。全 LIBERO-Plus benchmark 评估。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    libero_plus_overall: 78.9\n    libero_plus_std: 1.2\n    per_type_visual: 81.2\n    per_type_spatial: 77.5\n    per_type_physical: 74.8\n    per_subtype_camera: 78.5\n    per_subtype_light: 83.8\n    per_subtype_background: 80.2\n    per_subtype_noise: 82.1\n    per_subtype_layout: 77.5\n    per_subtype_robot: 74.8\n    routing_weight_visual_on_lora_v: 0.91\n    routing_weight_spatial_on_lora_s: 0.88\n    routing_weight_physical_on_lora_p: 0.86\n    routing_entropy_visual: 0.12\n    routing_entropy_spatial: 0.15\n    routing_entropy_physical: 0.18\n    par_routing_accuracy: 96.8\n    e2e_finetuning_epochs: 5\n    total_trainable_params_M: 11.6\n  result_rationale: '78.9% 整体成功率来自三个因素的协同：(1) PAR router routing accuracy 达 96.8%——\n    Phase 0 已证明 layer 6 first-token 激活在 3-class 上 F1=1.0，端到端微调只需 轻微校准 soft routing\n    的温度参数；(2) soft routing entropy 极低（0.12-0.18）， 说明 router 对每种扰动类型高度确信，routing weights\n    近似 one-hot（视觉扰动时 LoRA-V 权重 0.91），使 Meta-Brain 在运行时近似 oracle routing——这直接解释了 oracle\n    gap 仅 1.8pp；(3) 各 expert 本身质量高（plan_002 验证），routing 只需 选对 expert 即可。per-type 排序\n    V>S>P（81.2>77.5>74.8）反映了扰动修正的内在 难度梯度：视觉扰动是最规则的低秩变换（brightness/contrast 近似线性），空间扰动\n    需要调整 mid-level spatial reasoning，物理扰动涉及 action planning 的高层语义 重构。per-subtype 中\n    light 最高（83.8%）因为亮度变化是最平滑的视觉扰动， camera 稍低（78.5%）因为视角变化需要更复杂的几何 re-projection。Physical\n    expert 的 routing confidence 稍低（0.86 vs 0.91）因为物理扰动在激活空间中的 cluster 略松散（Phase 0:\n    physical F1=0.951 at K=1 vs spatial F1=1.0）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: LIBERO-Plus per-perturbation breakdown\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Perturbation\n      - Type\n      - Success (%)\n      - Δ Frozen (pp)\n      - Routing Weight\n      rows:\n      - - Camera\n        - Visual\n        - '78.5'\n        - '+30.3'\n        - 'LoRA-V: 0.92'\n      - - Light\n        - Visual\n        - '83.8'\n        - '+31.3'\n        - 'LoRA-V: 0.93'\n      - - Background\n        - Visual\n        - '80.2'\n        - '+29.4'\n        - 'LoRA-V: 0.90'\n      - - Noise\n        - Visual\n        - '82.1'\n        - '+28.9'\n        - 'LoRA-V: 0.89'\n      - - Layout\n        - Spatial\n        - '77.5'\n        - '+20.0'\n        - 'LoRA-S: 0.88'\n      - - Robot\n        - Physical\n        - '74.8'\n        - '+18.6'\n        - 'LoRA-P: 0.86'\n      - - Overall\n        - —\n        - '78.9'\n        - '+25.3'\n        - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'PAR routing weight heatmap 3×3: rows=input perturbation type, cols=LoRA expert,\n    near-diagonal structure'\n  - 'Per-subtype grouped bar chart: Meta-Brain vs Frozen pi0, gain annotated'\n  analysis: '78.9% overall + near-diagonal routing weights + 96.8% routing accuracy\n    共同 构成 best 档核心证据。routing entropy 的 per-type 差异（0.12 visual vs 0.18 physical）反映了\n    Phase 0 分类精度的差异——但即使 physical 的 entropy 也远低于 maximum（0.18 vs log(3)=1.10），确认所有类型的\n    routing 都高度确定。\n\n    '\n- name: Oracle Routing Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '用 ground-truth 扰动类型标签（hard one-hot）替换 PAR router，测量 learned routing\n    与 perfect routing 的上界差距。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    oracle_overall: 80.7\n    oracle_std: 0.9\n    oracle_visual: 83.0\n    oracle_spatial: 79.2\n    oracle_physical: 76.5\n    oracle_minus_meta_brain_overall: 1.8\n    oracle_minus_meta_brain_visual: 1.8\n    oracle_minus_meta_brain_spatial: 1.7\n    oracle_minus_meta_brain_physical: 1.7\n  result_rationale: 'Oracle routing 达到 80.7%，仅比 Meta-Brain（78.9%）高 1.8pp。Gap 小于 routing\n    分类错误率所预测的值（routing accuracy 96.8% → 3.2% 错误 → 预期 impact ~3pp）， 因为 PAR 的 soft routing\n    在分类不完全正确时仍分配了较高权重给正确 expert （如 misrouted visual 案例中 LoRA-V 仍获 0.65 权重 vs LoRA-S\n    0.35），使得 routing error 的 downstream impact 被 dampen。per-type gap 高度一致 （1.7-1.8pp），说明\n    PAR router 在三种类型上的性能均衡，没有系统性偏向。 Physical 的 oracle gap（1.7pp）最小，看似反直觉（physical\n    的 routing accuracy 最低），但 physical expert 的 cross-type performance（60.0-60.8%）高于其他\n    expert 的 cross-type（58.2-62.0%），使得 misrouting 的惩罚较轻。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: Meta-Brain vs Oracle per-type, error bars from 5 seeds, gap annotated'\n  analysis: '1.8pp gap 证明 PAR router 不是系统瓶颈。未来提升应聚焦于 expert 质量 （更好训练数据、更高 rank）而非\n    router 改进。Oracle 结果也为 routing 设定了 performance ceiling：~80.7% 是 rank-16 expert\n    bank 的理论上限。\n\n    '\n- name: Ablation Ladder — Full Systematic Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'LIBERO-Plus 上 6 个系统配置的系统对比（5 seeds）：Frozen → Universal-r16 → Universal-r48\n    → Random Routing → Meta-Brain → Oracle。包含 rank-48 parameter-matched control 和\n    random routing baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    frozen_pi0_overall: 53.6\n    frozen_pi0_std: 0.8\n    universal_r16_overall: 62.4\n    universal_r16_std: 1.4\n    universal_r48_overall: 65.1\n    universal_r48_std: 1.3\n    random_routing_overall: 65.8\n    random_routing_std: 2.1\n    meta_brain_overall: 78.9\n    meta_brain_std: 1.2\n    oracle_routing_overall: 80.7\n    oracle_routing_std: 0.9\n    step_frozen_to_r16: 8.8\n    step_r16_to_r48: 2.7\n    step_r48_to_random: 0.7\n    step_random_to_meta_brain: 13.1\n    step_meta_brain_to_oracle: 1.8\n    routing_gap_vs_rank48: 13.8\n    routing_gap_vs_random: 13.1\n    random_vs_r48_pvalue: 0.38\n    meta_brain_vs_random_pvalue: 3.0e-05\n    meta_brain_vs_r48_pvalue: 1.0e-05\n    per_type_visual_frozen: 50.8\n    per_type_spatial_frozen: 57.5\n    per_type_physical_frozen: 56.2\n    per_type_visual_r48: 67.5\n    per_type_spatial_r48: 63.2\n    per_type_physical_r48: 60.8\n    per_type_visual_random: 66.8\n    per_type_spatial_random: 65.5\n    per_type_physical_random: 63.2\n  result_rationale: '消融梯度严格单调递增（53.6→62.4→65.1→65.8→78.9→80.7），每一步对应一个 独立的能力维度： (1)\n    Frozen→r16（+8.8pp）：LoRA 本身提供了通用的 representation correction 能力， 即使不区分扰动类型，低秩修正也能改善\n    feature robustness。 (2) r16→r48（+2.7pp）：增加 rank 有帮助但收益递减——3.2× 参数仅换来 2.7pp， 说明\n    universal correction 的 capacity utilization efficiency 随 rank 下降， 因为额外参数被迫在三种互斥修正方向上妥协。\n    (3) r48→Random（+0.7pp, p=0.38 不显著）：仅 3 个 expert 的 ensemble 效应 几乎不存在。Random routing\n    有时碰巧选对 expert（1/3 概率），拉高了均值， 但也有 2/3 概率选错并导致 suboptimal correction。这两个效应近似抵消，\n    使 random 仅比 universal 高 0.7pp。p=0.38 的不显著性是关键 null result—— 它排除了 \"Meta-Brain 的好处来自\n    ensemble averaging\" 的 alternative explanation。 (4) Random→Meta-Brain（+13.1pp,\n    p<0.001）：整个梯度中最大的单步跳跃。 精确 routing 带来的提升远超 capacity scaling（2.7pp）和 ensemble（0.7pp）的\n    总和——routing 的边际贡献（13.1pp）是 capacity scaling（2.7pp）的 4.9×。 这是 Claim 2 的核心量化证据。\n    (5) Meta-Brain→Oracle（+1.8pp）：PAR router 接近理论上限。 Random routing 的高 std（2.1 vs\n    Meta-Brain 的 1.2）反映了随机 expert 分配的 天然不稳定性——在某些 seed 下碰巧匹配较多，在其他 seed 下则严重不匹配。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Ablation Ladder — Main Results (5 seeds)\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Method\n      - Params\n      - Overall (%)\n      - Visual (%)\n      - Spatial (%)\n      - Physical (%)\n      - Δ Frozen\n      rows:\n      - - Frozen pi0\n        - '0'\n        - 53.6 ± 0.8\n        - '50.8'\n        - '57.5'\n        - '56.2'\n        - —\n      - - Universal r16\n        - 3.7M\n        - 62.4 ± 1.4\n        - '64.8'\n        - '60.5'\n        - '58.2'\n        - '+8.8'\n      - - Universal r48\n        - 12M\n        - 65.1 ± 1.3\n        - '67.5'\n        - '63.2'\n        - '60.8'\n        - '+11.5'\n      - - Random Routing\n        - 12M\n        - 65.8 ± 2.1\n        - '66.8'\n        - '65.5'\n        - '63.2'\n        - '+12.2'\n      - - Meta-Brain (ours)\n        - 12M\n        - 78.9 ± 1.2\n        - '81.2'\n        - '77.5'\n        - '74.8'\n        - '+25.3'\n      - - Oracle Routing\n        - 12M\n        - 80.7 ± 0.9\n        - '83.0'\n        - '79.2'\n        - '76.5'\n        - '+27.1'\n  - name: Statistical significance\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Comparison\n      - Gap (pp)\n      - p-value\n      - Significant?\n      rows:\n      - - Meta-Brain vs r48\n        - '13.8'\n        - <0.001\n        - Yes (***)\n      - - Meta-Brain vs Random\n        - '13.1'\n        - <0.001\n        - Yes (***)\n      - - Random vs r48\n        - '0.7'\n        - '0.38'\n        - No (n.s.)\n      - - Oracle vs Meta-Brain\n        - '1.8'\n        - '0.03'\n        - Yes (*)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 6 bars in ablation order, color-coded cold→warm, 5-seed error bars,\n    significance brackets'\n  - 'Decomposition pie chart: routing contribution (13.1pp) vs capacity (2.7pp) vs\n    ensemble (0.7pp) vs baseline (8.8pp)'\n  analysis: '消融梯度提供三个推论：(a) routing >> ensemble（13.1pp vs 0.7pp, ratio 18.7×）； (b)\n    routing >> capacity scaling（13.8pp vs 2.7pp, ratio 5.1×）； (c) PAR ≈ oracle（gap\n    1.8pp）。Random vs r48 的 null result（p=0.38）是 全文最关键的 negative finding——它排除了 Claim\n    2 的唯一 alternative explanation。\n\n    '\n- name: FTM/FLA Reproduction — Visual-Only Baseline\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '在 pi0 backbone 上复现 FTM（Fine-Tuning Masking），对比 FTM vs Meta-Brain 在视觉扰动上的表现，并展示\n    Meta-Brain 在 spatial/physical 上的独特优势。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ftm_visual_avg: 75.7\n    ftm_camera: 73.2\n    ftm_light: 78.5\n    ftm_background: 74.8\n    ftm_noise: 76.2\n    ftm_spatial: 55.8\n    ftm_physical: 54.5\n    ftm_overall: 65.2\n    ftm_params_K: 4\n    meta_brain_vs_ftm_visual_gap: 5.5\n    meta_brain_vs_ftm_spatial_gap: 21.7\n    meta_brain_vs_ftm_physical_gap: 20.3\n  result_rationale: 'FTM 在 pi0 上复现后视觉扰动达 75.7%（+24.9pp over frozen），以极少参数（4K） 实现了可观修正，验证了\n    FTM 的 feature masking 原理在 pi0 上同样有效—— masking 通过抑制 early-layer 中被扰动 corrupted\n    的 feature channel 来恢复 clean representation。但 FTM 在 spatial（55.8%）和 physical（54.5%）上等同于\n    frozen baseline 甚至略低（spatial -1.7pp），因为 FTM 的核心假设是扰动破坏 视觉特征——对 layout 变化或机器人初始状态变化，masking\n    visual channels 不仅 无益反而可能抑制有用的 spatial/physical 信号。Meta-Brain 在视觉扰动上也高于 FTM（81.2%\n    vs 75.7%，+5.5pp），因为 rank-16 LoRA（3.7M params）比 feature masking（4K params）有更大的修正表达能力——LoRA\n    可以 rotate 和 scale 整个 subspace，而 masking 只能 zero-out channels。但 FTM 的极高参数效率 （4K\n    params for +24.9pp on visual）使其在 visual-only 场景下仍然有独特价值。 核心对比：Meta-Brain 在 spatial/physical\n    上分别高出 FTM 21.7pp 和 20.3pp， 这正是 multi-type routing 的 unique value proposition。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: FTM vs Meta-Brain comparison\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Method\n      - Params\n      - Visual (%)\n      - Spatial (%)\n      - Physical (%)\n      - Overall (%)\n      rows:\n      - - Frozen pi0\n        - '0'\n        - '50.8'\n        - '57.5'\n        - '56.2'\n        - '53.6'\n      - - FTM (reprod.)\n        - 4K\n        - '75.7'\n        - '55.8'\n        - '54.5'\n        - '65.2'\n      - - Meta-Brain\n        - 12M\n        - '81.2'\n        - '77.5'\n        - '74.8'\n        - '78.9'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: Visual/Spatial/Physical, 3 bars each (Frozen, FTM, Meta-Brain),\n    showing FTM''s visual-only strength'\n  analysis: 'FTM 是 visual-only robustness 的 strong baseline，且参数效率极高。论文中应定位为 \"single-modality\n    approach 的代表\"——它证明了 visual 修正可以极其高效， 但也证明了 single-modality 无法推广到 multi-type perturbation\n    场景。 Meta-Brain 即使在 visual-only 上也优于 FTM（+5.5pp），说明 LoRA-based correction 比 feature\n    masking 更有表达力。\n\n    '\n- name: Parameter Efficiency Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '计算各方法的 gain-over-frozen-baseline，按可训练参数归一化， 绘制 parameter efficiency\n    scatter plot。纯分析，无 GPU 计算。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    meta_brain_gain_pp: 25.3\n    meta_brain_params_M: 12\n    meta_brain_gain_per_M: 2.11\n    universal_r16_gain_pp: 8.8\n    universal_r16_params_M: 3.7\n    universal_r16_gain_per_M: 2.38\n    universal_r48_gain_pp: 11.5\n    universal_r48_params_M: 12\n    universal_r48_gain_per_M: 0.96\n    ftm_gain_visual_pp: 24.9\n    ftm_gain_overall_pp: 11.6\n    ftm_params_M: 0.004\n    ftm_gain_per_M_visual: 6225.0\n    ftm_gain_per_M_overall: 2900.0\n    vla_gse_gain_pp: 12.0\n    vla_gse_params_M: 114\n    vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.105\n    meta_brain_pareto_optimal: true\n    meta_brain_vs_r48_efficiency_ratio: 2.2\n  result_rationale: '参数效率分析揭示了三个 regime：(1) 极低参数区（<1M）：FTM 以 4K params 在 visual-only\n    上达到 gain_per_M=6225，但 overall gain_per_M（2900）反映了它 无法覆盖 non-visual 的局限；(2) 中等参数区（1-15M）：Meta-Brain\n    占据 Pareto 前沿——12M params, 25.3pp gain, gain_per_M=2.11。同参数量的 Universal-r48 仅 gain_per_M=0.96，效率差\n    2.2×。这 2.2× 的效率倍数就是 routing 的量化贡献； (3) 高参数区（>100M）：VLA-GSE 的 114M params 仅提供 gain_per_M=0.105\n    （不同 backbone，仅作 suggestive 对比）。即使考虑 backbone 差异，Meta-Brain 的 gain_per_M（2.11）比\n    VLA-GSE（0.105）高 20×，数量级差异足以支撑 parameter efficiency narrative。Universal r16 的 gain_per_M（2.38）看似高于\n    Meta-Brain （2.11），但绝对 gain 仅 8.8pp vs 25.3pp——在 \"达到实用性能阈值\" 的约束下， r16 的高效率无意义，因为\n    62.4% 可能低于部署要求。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Parameter efficiency summary\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Method\n      - Backbone\n      - Params\n      - Gain (pp)\n      - Gain/M\n      - Coverage\n      rows:\n      - - FTM\n        - pi0\n        - 4K\n        - +24.9 (V) / +11.6 (all)\n        - 6225 / 2900\n        - Visual only\n      - - Universal r16\n        - pi0\n        - 3.7M\n        - '+8.8'\n        - '2.38'\n        - All types\n      - - Meta-Brain (ours)\n        - pi0\n        - 12M\n        - '+25.3'\n        - '2.11'\n        - All types\n      - - Universal r48\n        - pi0\n        - 12M\n        - '+11.5'\n        - '0.96'\n        - All types\n      - - VLA-GSE †\n        - Qwen3-4B\n        - 114M\n        - '+12.0'\n        - '0.105'\n        - All types\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: x=trainable params (log scale), y=gain-over-frozen (pp). Meta-Brain\n    on Pareto front. FTM in ultra-low-param corner. VLA-GSE in high-param low-efficiency\n    region (dashed circle, different backbone). Isoquants of gain_per_M as diagonal\n    lines.'\n  analysis: 'Meta-Brain 是 multi-type robustness 场景下的 Pareto optimal 方法。关键 insight：\n    routing 让同等参数预算（12M）的效率提升 2.2×——这不是 architectural overhead 的代价，而是 capacity allocation\n    strategy 的收益。Parameter efficiency scatter 是 Claim 3 的 primary visual evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: Correction Memory Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: '对比 Meta-Brain with/without Correction Memory (CM)，量化 CM 的边际收益。 CM\n    通过 FAISS 检索相似历史扰动的 routing weight 来调制当前 routing。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    meta_brain_no_cm: 78.9\n    meta_brain_with_cm: 80.1\n    cm_delta_overall: 1.2\n    cm_delta_visual: 0.8\n    cm_delta_spatial: 1.5\n    cm_delta_physical: 1.8\n    cm_additional_params: 1\n    cm_latency_overhead_ms: 2.3\n    cm_pvalue: 0.08\n  result_rationale: 'CM 提供 +1.2pp 整体提升（p=0.08, borderline significant with 5 seeds），\n    主要来自 spatial（+1.5pp）和 physical（+1.8pp）而非 visual（+0.8pp）。 这符合 CM 的设计逻辑：CM 检索与当前\n    observation 最相似的历史扰动 exemplar， 用其 routing weight 作为 contextual prior 来调制 PAR 输出。Spatial\n    和 physical 扰动的 within-type 变异更大（不同 layout randomization 的具体形态差异远大于 不同 lighting\n    condition），历史 exemplar 能提供有用的 \"这种具体 layout 变化 应该如何调整 routing\" 的信息。Visual 上 CM\n    收益小因为 PAR 对视觉扰动已经 足够准确（routing accuracy ~98% on visual），contextual modulation\n    的改进空间 有限。但 +1.2pp 的总收益与 1 个额外可学习参数 + 2.3ms CPU latency 相比， cost-benefit 偏低——不值得作为\n    named architectural component 推广。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Ablation bar chart: with/without CM, per-type Δ annotated, p-value shown'\n  analysis: 'CM 是 optional module，+1.2pp 不改变任何 claim 的结论。论文呈现策略： 一行 ablation 文字 +\n    footnote table，明确标注 \"optional, borderline significant\"。 Dream reviewers 一致认为 CM\n    是 padding，降级处理是正确决策。\n\n    '\n- name: Router Architecture Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '对比 3 种 PAR router 变体：2-layer MLP (default), linear classifier, attention-based\n    router。均使用 PaliGemma layer 6 first-token features。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mlp_routing_accuracy: 96.8\n    mlp_downstream: 78.9\n    mlp_params_M: 0.53\n    linear_routing_accuracy: 94.2\n    linear_downstream: 76.8\n    linear_params_M: 0.01\n    attention_routing_accuracy: 97.1\n    attention_downstream: 78.5\n    attention_params_M: 1.85\n  result_rationale: 'MLP（96.8% routing, 78.9% downstream）是最优 cost-performance 均衡。Linear\n    分类器准确率低 2.6pp（94.2%），因为 3-class 边界在激活空间中有轻微非线性—— Phase 0 t-SNE 显示 Spatial/Physical\n    cluster 的边界不完全线性可分（两者都 影响 action space，共享部分特征），MLP 的一层隐藏层足以 model 这个非线性。 2.6pp\n    routing gap 转化为 2.1pp downstream gap（76.8% vs 78.9%），说明 routing accuracy 和 task\n    success 近似线性相关但有 damping（soft routing 缓冲了部分 routing error）。Attention-based router\n    routing accuracy 最高 （97.1%），但 downstream 反而略低（78.5%），因为 1.85M 额外参数在仅 5 epoch 微调下轻微\n    overfit——attention 的表达能力对 3-class routing 过剩。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Router architecture comparison\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Router Type\n      - Params (M)\n      - Routing Acc (%)\n      - Downstream (%)\n      rows:\n      - - Linear\n        - '0.01'\n        - '94.2'\n        - '76.8'\n      - - 2-layer MLP ★\n        - '0.53'\n        - '96.8'\n        - '78.9'\n      - - Attention\n        - '1.85'\n        - '97.1'\n        - '78.5'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Router 架构的 downstream impact 有限（max spread 2.1pp），说明 Meta-Brain 的性能主要由\n    routing 原理和 expert 质量驱动，而非 router 实现细节。 论文中作简短 ablation paragraph 处理。\n\n    '\n- name: 6-class vs 3-class Routing\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '对比 6-class 精细路由（camera/light/background/noise/layout/robot 各一个 LoRA\n    expert，6×3.7M=22.1M params）vs 3-class 粗路由（Visual/Spatial/Physical， 3×3.7M=11.1M\n    params）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    3class_overall: 78.9\n    3class_params_M: 12\n    6class_overall: 79.6\n    6class_params_M: 24\n    6class_delta: 0.7\n    6class_camera: 80.2\n    6class_light: 84.5\n    6class_background: 81.0\n    6class_noise: 83.2\n    6class_layout: 77.8\n    6class_robot: 75.1\n    marginal_gain_per_expert: 0.23\n    6class_routing_accuracy: 94.8\n  result_rationale: '6-class 仅比 3-class 高 0.7pp（79.6% vs 78.9%），参数量翻倍（24M vs 12M），\n    每额外 expert 的边际收益仅 0.23pp。这与 Phase 0 的发现一致：intra-Visual 4 个 sub-type 在激活空间中形成一个紧致\n    cluster（6-class accuracy 99.8% 但 sub-type 间 cosine similarity 高达 0.92），说明 camera/light/background/noise\n    的修正策略高度重叠——它们都影响 early-layer visual representation，差异更多是 程度而非类型。Independent camera\n    expert 比 shared LoRA-V 仅高 1.7pp（80.2% vs 78.5%），代价是独占 3.7M 参数。同时 6-class routing\n    accuracy 下降到 94.8% （vs 3-class 96.8%），因为 6-class 边界更精细，分类更困难，少量 routing error\n    部分抵消了 expert specialization 的收益。3-class 是 granularity 的 sweet spot。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Granularity comparison\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Granularity\n      - Experts\n      - Total Params\n      - Overall (%)\n      - Routing Acc (%)\n      - Δ\n      rows:\n      - - 3-class\n        - '3'\n        - 12M\n        - '78.9'\n        - '96.8'\n        - —\n      - - 6-class\n        - '6'\n        - 24M\n        - '79.6'\n        - '94.8'\n        - '+0.7'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '0.7pp / 2× params 的 trade-off 验证了 3-class taxonomy 的合理性，回应 Reviewer C5。Phase\n    0 的 Visual cluster 紧致性是根本原因——finer granularity within Visual 增加 routing 难度但不增加修正多样性。\n\n    '\n- name: Rank-48 Parameter-Matched Universal LoRA — Existential Control\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: '训练 rank-48 universal LoRA（~11.1M params，精确匹配 Meta-Brain 的 3×rank-16\n    expert 参数总量）。若 rank-48 ≈ Meta-Brain → Claim 2 崩溃。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    rank48_overall: 65.1\n    rank48_std: 1.3\n    rank48_visual: 67.5\n    rank48_spatial: 63.2\n    rank48_physical: 60.8\n    rank48_vs_meta_brain_gap: 13.8\n    rank48_vs_r16_improvement: 2.7\n    rank48_gain_over_frozen: 11.5\n    rank48_gain_per_M: 0.96\n    claim2_survival: true\n  result_rationale: 'Rank-48 universal LoRA 达到 65.1%（+11.5pp over frozen），仅比 rank-16\n    （62.4%）高 2.7pp，despite 3.2× 参数增长（3.7M → 11.1M）。这证实了 \"universal capacity saturation\"\n    假设：uniform LoRA 的收益在 rank 16-48 之间快速递减。根本原因：rank-48 的 11.1M 参数被迫在三种修正方向（visual:\n    early-layer re-projection, spatial: mid-layer trajectory adjustment, physical:\n    late-layer action re-planning）之间共享。这三种修正在 representation space 中 方向不同甚至互斥——改善\n    visual robustness 的 rank 方向可能削弱 spatial 性能。 增加 rank 只是增加了妥协的参数量，无法解决方向冲突。per-type\n    分布清晰展示了 这个困境：Visual（67.5%）的 gain over frozen（+16.7pp）远大于 Spatial（+5.7pp） 和 Physical（+4.6pp），因为\n    visual perturbation 在混合训练数据中占 4/6 sub-types， universal LoRA 被 biased toward visual\n    correction。Meta-Brain 的 3 experts 各自专注一种类型，消除了方向冲突和数据 imbalance。13.8pp gap（p<0.001）\n    是 Claim 2 的 existential validation：identical parameter budget, dramatically different\n    outcome。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Embedded in ablation ladder figure: rank-48 bar annotated with ''= Meta-Brain\n    params'' and 13.8pp gap arrow'\n  analysis: '全文最关键的单个实验。13.8pp gap + p<0.001 直接证明 routing 的价值不可被 parameter scaling\n    替代。如果这个 gap <5pp，整篇论文的 thesis 就需要根本性重构。 在 best 档下，gap 足够大且稳健，Claim 2 完整存活。\n\n    '\n- name: LoRA Rank Sweep (r=16/32/64)\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: '在 r=16/32/64 三个 expert rank 上分别训练 Meta-Brain 和 parameter-matched universal\n    LoRA，测试 routing benefit 是否随 expert capacity 增长而变化。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r16_meta_brain: 78.9\n    r16_universal_matched: 65.1\n    r16_routing_benefit: 13.8\n    r16_total_params_M: 12\n    r32_meta_brain: 81.5\n    r32_universal_matched: 67.6\n    r32_routing_benefit: 13.9\n    r32_total_params_M: 24\n    r64_meta_brain: 84.2\n    r64_universal_matched: 70.0\n    r64_routing_benefit: 14.2\n    r64_total_params_M: 48\n    benefit_trend: monotonically increasing\n    universal_diminishing_returns_r48_to_r96: 2.5\n    universal_diminishing_returns_r96_to_r192: 2.4\n  result_rationale: 'Routing benefit 单调递增（13.8→13.9→14.2pp），排除了 Dream worst-case \"routing\n    benefit 仅在特定 capacity 下出现\" 的顾虑。递增的机制： (1) 更高 rank 的 expert 能捕获更精细的 type-specific\n    correction（r=64 LoRA-V on visual ~86%），这些精细修正的价值在 universal setting 下被 dilute\n    掉—— universal 必须在三种修正之间分配每一个 rank component。 (2) Universal LoRA 的 scaling 呈递减：r48→r96\n    仅 +2.5pp, r96→r192 仅 +2.4pp， 因为额外 rank 被用于 refine 已有的妥协方案，而非学习新的修正维度。 (3) Meta-Brain\n    的 scaling 近似线性（78.9→81.5→84.2，每次 ~+2.6pp）， 因为每个 expert 的额外 rank 直接用于 deepen 该类型的专有修正，没有\n    cross-type interference。两条 scaling curve 的斜率差导致 benefit gap 缓慢扩大。 这个 finding 的叙事意义：routing\n    benefit 不是特定 capacity 的 artifact， 而是 fundamental architectural advantage——无论参数预算大小，routing\n    始终优于 uniform correction。如果有更多参数预算，应投入到更高 rank 的 routed experts。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Rank sweep results\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Expert Rank\n      - Meta-Brain (%)\n      - Matched Universal (%)\n      - Routing Benefit (pp)\n      - Total Params\n      rows:\n      - - r=16\n        - '78.9'\n        - '65.1'\n        - '13.8'\n        - 12M\n      - - r=32\n        - '81.5'\n        - '67.6'\n        - '13.9'\n        - 24M\n      - - r=64\n        - '84.2'\n        - '70.0'\n        - '14.2'\n        - 48M\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: x=rank (log scale), y=success rate. Two lines (Meta-Brain, Universal),\n    diverging gap annotated at each rank'\n  analysis: 'Monotonically increasing routing benefit 是一个 clean scaling result。 它也暗示\n    r=64 Meta-Brain（84.2%）可以 match 或超过 VLA-GSE（81.2%，不同 backbone），虽然 cross-backbone\n    对比是 indirect，但趋势线的 extrapolation 支持 Meta-Brain 在更高 capacity 下的 competitive potential。\n\n    '\n- name: Clean LIBERO Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: '在标准（无扰动）LIBERO 上评估 Meta-Brain 和 baselines，验证 routing 不会 降低 nominal\n    performance。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    frozen_pi0_clean: 91.2\n    universal_r16_clean: 90.8\n    universal_r48_clean: 90.5\n    meta_brain_clean: 91.5\n    clean_delta_meta_brain: 0.3\n    clean_delta_r16: -0.4\n    clean_delta_r48: -0.7\n    par_routing_entropy_on_clean: 0.85\n    par_routing_weight_distribution_clean: ≈ 0.34/0.33/0.33\n  result_rationale: 'Meta-Brain 在 clean LIBERO 上 91.5%（Δ=+0.3pp vs frozen），完全保持 nominal\n    性能。这得益于 PAR router 的一个 emergent 行为：在无扰动输入下，layer 6 first-token 激活不匹配任何已知扰动 pattern，PAR\n    输出高 entropy（0.85， 接近 max log(3)=1.10），routing weights 近似均匀（~0.33/0.33/0.33）。 三个\n    expert 的修正在 clean input 上大致方向相反（各自 tuned 为不同扰动的 correction），均匀加权后 net correction\n    ≈ 0——routing 自动 degrade to identity。微弱的 +0.3pp 正 delta 可能来自 expert LoRA 的轻微 regularization\n    效果。对比 Universal LoRA：r16 下降 0.4pp, r48 下降 0.7pp，因为 universal LoRA 始终应用 correction（无\n    \"关闭\" 机制），对 clean input 造成不必要的 representation perturbation。Rank 越高干扰越大（r48 的 -0.7pp），因为\n    higher-rank LoRA 的 representation 修改幅度更大。这为 deployment 增加了 重要论据：Meta-Brain 的 routing\n    机制在正常条件下安全 graceful degrade， 而 always-on universal correction 有代价。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Clean LIBERO preservation\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Method\n      - Clean LIBERO (%)\n      - Δ vs Frozen (pp)\n      rows:\n      - - Frozen pi0\n        - '91.2'\n        - —\n      - - Universal r16\n        - '90.8'\n        - '-0.4'\n      - - Universal r48\n        - '90.5'\n        - '-0.7'\n      - - Meta-Brain\n        - '91.5'\n        - '+0.3'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Clean LIBERO preservation 是 practical deployment argument 的关键证据。 Meta-Brain\n    是唯一在 perturbed 和 clean 条件下都不降级的方法。PAR routing 的 high-entropy fallback 是一个 emergent\n    property（非刻意设计），可作为 \"routing 自动 detect perturbation absence\" 的附加 insight 呈现。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Backbone Validation (SmolVLA)\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: '在 SmolVLA 上复现 Phase 0 + Phase 1 核心 pipeline，验证 perturbation-diagnostic\n    routing 的跨架构泛化性。P2 优先级。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    smolvla_phase0_3class_f1: 0.971\n    smolvla_phase0_best_layer: 4\n    smolvla_frozen_libero_plus: 49.8\n    smolvla_universal_r16: 58.2\n    smolvla_meta_brain: 72.4\n    smolvla_gain_over_frozen: 22.6\n    smolvla_routing_benefit_vs_universal: 14.2\n    smolvla_routing_accuracy: 94.5\n  result_rationale: 'SmolVLA Phase 0 F1=0.971（vs pi0 0.993），略低但仍极高，验证了 perturbation\n    diagnosability 不是 PaliGemma 架构的特有属性。Best layer 是 layer 4 （SmolVLA 共 ~12 层），深度比例\n    ~1/3 与 pi0 的 layer 6/18 一致， 暗示 perturbation information 在 VLA 中的 consolidation\n    发生在相对一致的 depth fraction。Phase 0 F1 略低的原因：SmolVLA 的 representation 维度更小， perturbation\n    cluster 间的 margin 更窄，但仍足以支撑高质量 routing。 Meta-Brain on SmolVLA 达到 72.4%（+22.6pp\n    over frozen 49.8%）， routing benefit vs universal 为 14.2pp（vs pi0 上的 13.8pp），定量吻合度很高。\n    SmolVLA 绝对性能低于 pi0（72.4% vs 78.9%）因为 backbone capacity 更小， 但 routing benefit 的相对大小几乎相同（14.2\n    vs 13.8），说明 routing 的价值不依赖于 backbone quality——无论 backbone 强弱， perturbation-type-specific\n    correction 都比 uniform correction 更高效。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-backbone comparison\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Metric\n      - pi0 (PaliGemma)\n      - SmolVLA\n      rows:\n      - - Phase 0 3-class F1\n        - '0.993'\n        - '0.971'\n      - - Best probing layer\n        - 6 / 18\n        - 4 / 12\n      - - Frozen baseline (%)\n        - '53.6'\n        - '49.8'\n      - - Universal r16 (%)\n        - '62.4'\n        - '58.2'\n      - - Meta-Brain (%)\n        - '78.9'\n        - '72.4'\n      - - Routing benefit (pp)\n        - '13.8'\n        - '14.2'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: pi0 vs SmolVLA, routing benefit annotated, showing consistency'\n  analysis: 'Cross-backbone validation 将 contribution 从 \"pi0 上有效的 technique\" 提升为 \"VLA\n    的通用 robustness principle\"。routing benefit 在两个 backbone 上的 高度一致性（13.8 vs 14.2pp）是最有说服力的\n    generalization evidence。 直接回应 Reviewer C3。\n\n    '\n- name: LoRA Layer Placement Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: '对比不同 PaliGemma 层覆盖范围（early 2-6, mid 6-12, late 12-16, all 2-16） 对各\n    expert type 的影响。P2 优先级。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    lora_v_early: 78.5\n    lora_v_mid: 76.2\n    lora_v_late: 72.8\n    lora_v_all: 80.2\n    lora_s_early: 73.5\n    lora_s_mid: 76.8\n    lora_s_late: 74.2\n    lora_s_all: 77.5\n    lora_p_early: 69.8\n    lora_p_mid: 72.5\n    lora_p_late: 74.5\n    lora_p_all: 74.8\n    v_best_subset: early (2-6)\n    s_best_subset: mid (6-12)\n    p_best_subset: late (12-16)\n    v_all_minus_best_subset: 1.7\n    s_all_minus_best_subset: 0.7\n    p_all_minus_best_subset: 0.3\n  result_rationale: 'Layer placement 揭示了清晰的 V→early, S→mid, P→late 偏好梯度： LoRA-V 在\n    early layers 最优 subset（78.5%），因为视觉扰动（camera/light/ background/noise）破坏 early visual\n    representation——在损坏发生处修正最高效。 Late layers（72.8%）最差（-7.4pp vs all），因为 corrupted\n    features 已经 propagate 到深层并 compound，late-layer 修正无法 undo upstream corruption。\n    LoRA-S 在 mid layers 最优（76.8%），因为 spatial perturbation（layout 变化） 影响的是 visual-to-spatial\n    reasoning 的转换阶段——mid layers 将 2D visual features 转化为 3D spatial-action representations。LoRA-P\n    在 late layers 最优（74.5%），且与 all-layer（74.8%）仅差 0.3pp，因为 physical perturbation （robot\n    初始状态变化）影响 high-level action planning，这发生在 late decision layers。但所有 expert 在 all-layer\n    覆盖下均为最优或接近最优，说明 cross-layer redundancy 有益——即使存在层偏好，拥有 all-layer coverage 可以 catch\n    residual perturbation effects at other layers。v_all_minus_best_subset 最大（1.7pp），\n    说明 visual perturbation 虽集中在 early layers 但 mid/late 仍有 residual impact。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Layer placement ablation\n    data:\n      headers:\n      - Layers\n      - LoRA-V Visual (%)\n      - LoRA-S Spatial (%)\n      - LoRA-P Physical (%)\n      rows:\n      - - Early (2-6)\n        - 78.5 ★V\n        - '73.5'\n        - '69.8'\n      - - Mid (6-12)\n        - '76.2'\n        - 76.8 ★S\n        - '72.5'\n      - - Late (12-16)\n        - '72.8'\n        - '74.2'\n        - 74.5 ★P\n      - - All (2-16)\n        - '80.2'\n        - '77.5'\n        - '74.8'\n  figures_description:\n  - '3×4 heatmap: rows=layer range, cols=expert type, ★=best subset per expert, diagonal\n    pattern visible'\n  analysis: V→early, S→mid, P→late 的对应关系提供了 mechanistic insight，支撑 \"不同扰动 影响不同处理阶段\"\n    的理论框架。这个 finding 虽然不影响主要 claim（all-layer 仍是实用最优），但作为 practical insight 增加了论文的理论深度。未来工作可\n    探索 layer-specific routing（根据扰动类型动态选择 active layers）。\n","numLines":958,"startLine":1,"totalLines":958}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017aprjwkYqvC57pdq9GP5jL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for 2026 appear to still be in development. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Resources\n\nThe search results also reference reviewer guidelines from previous CoRL conferences. For example, CoRL 2023 guidelines assessed papers on relevance (whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested).\n\nThe detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form appear to not yet be publicly available. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page or the main CoRL 2026 website for the most current reviewer guidelines and review form when they are released.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d09a97eb-2874-493a-b7bd-2546bcb68a45","uuid":"32d8a2f8-1f96-49d7-b9a5-4e76d08eb266","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:09:33.174Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016KWXwb5FPsDociqxJddmqm","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for 2026 appear to still be in development. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Resources\n\nThe search results also reference reviewer guidelines from previous CoRL conferences. For example, CoRL 2023 guidelines assessed papers on relevance (whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested).\n\nThe detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form appear to not yet be publicly available. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page or the main CoRL 2026 website for the most current reviewer guidelines and review form when they are released."],"durationSeconds":6.241276168999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01776XZ4m4UrnAtuQFUqHfG3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed guidance I could locate was from CoRL 2023 and 2024, rather than specific 2025 materials. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines Overview\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors and reflecting them strongly in scores.\n\n## Review Conduct\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nRegular paper submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Important Process Notes\n\nThe CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period. Papers under review are strictly confidential and should not be shared or discussed except with the Area Chair and Program Chairs.\n\nThe search results did not return a specific detailed CoRL 2025 review form with explicit scoring criteria values. For the most current and complete information about CoRL 2025 specific scoring criteria and review form details, you may want to check the OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 Conference directly or contact the conference organizers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d09a97eb-2874-493a-b7bd-2546bcb68a45","uuid":"0b752684-081d-4cdd-9a79-501aab3349e5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:09:33.991Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011D9k1SbZmGEKe5fvm4dYYW","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"}]},"Based on my search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed guidance I could locate was from CoRL 2023 and 2024, rather than specific 2025 materials. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines Overview\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors and reflecting them strongly in scores.\n\n## Review Conduct\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nRegular paper submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Important Process Notes\n\nThe CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period. Papers under review are strictly confidential and should not be shared or discussed except with the Area Chair and Program Chairs.\n\nThe search results did not return a specific detailed CoRL 2025 review form with explicit scoring criteria values. For the most current and complete information about CoRL 2025 specific scoring criteria and review form details, you may want to check the OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 Conference directly or contact the conference organizers."],"durationSeconds":6.567130