{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RXZodDkfKUh7qVHm79dexC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" review form scoring scale criteria site:2024.corl.org\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 \"Instruction for Reviews\" page. Here's what was retrieved:\n\nReview Criteria (for regular papers): Submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe page also covers desk rejection criteria, including:\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope.\n\nRegarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results show the beginning of the review criteria section, but the full content appears to be cut off. For the complete review form scoring scale criteria, you may need to visit the full page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d09a97eb-2874-493a-b7bd-2546bcb68a45","uuid":"5c7e2d49-c685-47e6-a9f4-37d16011eaca","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:09:44.709Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" review form scoring scale criteria site:2024.corl.org","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017kmXgL1NMvzdiGyH3d9g8W","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 \"Instruction for Reviews\" page. Here's what was retrieved:\n\nReview Criteria (for regular papers): Submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe page also covers desk rejection criteria, including:\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope.\n\nRegarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results show the beginning of the review criteria section, but the full content appears to be cut off. For the complete review form scoring scale criteria, you may need to visit the full page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews."],"durationSeconds":3.2014479390000017}}
