{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011oQT8Empm4zxtQHvY6wRuT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016xH4KfuHaHHSJe4YFCJzHk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus: **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Venue: CoRL 2026\n- Score scale: 1-10 (10=top 5% seminal, 9=top 15% strong accept, 8=top 50% clear accept, 7=good accept, 6=marginally above threshold, 5=marginally below threshold, 4=rejection, 3=clear rejection, 2=strong rejection, 1=trivial/wrong)\n- Acceptance rate ~30%. Papers must be relevant to robot learning.\n- Reviewers evaluate significance, novelty, soundness, clarity, reproducibility.\n\n## Paper: \"Meta-Brain: Perturbation-Diagnostic Routing of LoRA Experts for Robust Vision-Language-Action Models\"\n\n### Summary\nMeta-Brain diagnoses perturbation type from frozen VLA activations and routes to type-specialized LoRA experts. Key empirical finding: frozen PaliGemma layer 6 first-token activations achieve F1=1.0 on 3-class perturbation classification (visual/spatial/physical). A PAR router (2-layer MLP, 0.53M params) produces soft routing weights over 3 LoRA experts (LoRA-V, LoRA-S, LoRA-P, each rank-16, ~3.7M params). On LIBERO-Plus benchmark: Meta-Brain 78.9% vs parameter-matched universal LoRA r48 65.1% (+13.8pp, p<0.001). Random routing yields only 65.8% (+0.7pp over universal, p=0.38 n.s.), ruling out ensemble effects. Oracle gap only 1.8pp. Cross-backbone on SmolVLA: +14.2pp routing benefit. Clean LIBERO preserved (+0.3pp).\n\n### Method Details (Section 3)\n- Problem: frozen VLA fθ (pi0 + PaliGemma), perturbed obs õ_t = o_t + δ, δ ∈ {visual, spatial, physical}\n- Phase 0: KNN probing on layer 6 first-token activation → F1=1.0 at K=1\n- PAR: h^(6)_t[0] → 2-layer MLP → softmax → p=[pV, pS, pP]\n- ALB: h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ_k p_k · ΔW_k · h_frozen, where ΔW_k = B_k A_k (LoRA)\n- Training: (1) Each expert trained independently on matched perturbation type, 15 epochs. (2) Freeze LoRA, train PAR end-to-end on full LIBERO-Plus mix, 5 epochs. Total: ~11.6M params.\n\n### Experimental Results\n**Table 1 - Ablation Ladder (5 seeds):**\n| Method | Params | Overall (%) | Visual | Spatial | Physical |\n|--------|--------|------------|--------|---------|----------|\n| Frozen pi0 | 0 | 53.6±0.8 | 50.8 | 57.5 | 56.2 |\n| Universal r16 | 3.7M | 62.4±1.4 | 64.8 | 60.5 | 58.2 |\n| Universal r48 | 12M | 65.1±1.3 | 67.5 | 63.2 | 60.8 |\n| Random Routing | 12M | 65.8±2.1 | 66.8 | 65.5 | 63.2 |\n| Meta-Brain | 12M | 78.9±1.2 | 81.2 | 77.5 | 74.8 |\n| Oracle Routing | 12M | 80.7±0.9 | 83.0 | 79.2 | 76.5 |\n\n**Table 2 - Statistical significance:**\n- Meta-Brain vs r48: 13.8pp, p<0.001 (***)\n- Meta-Brain vs Random: 13.1pp, p<0.001 (***)\n- Random vs r48: 0.7pp, p=0.38 (n.s.)\n- Oracle vs Meta-Brain: 1.8pp, p=0.03 (*)\n\n**Table 3 - Per-perturbation:** All 6 subtypes show +18.6 to +31.3pp gains. Routing weights near-diagonal (0.86-0.93). Routing entropy low (0.12-0.18 vs max 1.10).\n\n**Table 4 - Cross-type matrix:** Avg cross-type drop 17.4pp, validating expert specialization.\n\n**Table 5 - FTM comparison:** FTM 75.7% visual but 55.8% spatial, 54.5% physical. Meta-Brain 81.2/77.5/74.8.\n\n**Table 6 - Rank sweep:** Routing benefit monotonically increasing (13.8→13.9→14.2pp at r=16/32/64).\n\n**Table 7 - Parameter efficiency:** Meta-Brain 2.11 pp/M, Universal r48 0.96 pp/M (2.2× ratio). VLA-GSE 0.105 pp/M (different backbone).\n\n**Table 8 - Clean LIBERO:** Meta-Brain 91.5% (+0.3pp), universal r16 -0.4pp, r48 -0.7pp.\n\n**Table 9 - Cross-backbone (SmolVLA):** F1=0.971, routing benefit +14.2pp (vs pi0's +13.8pp).\n\n**Table 10 - Router architecture:** Linear 76.8%, MLP 78.9%, Attention 78.5%. Narrow spread (2.1pp).\n\n**Table 11 - 6-class vs 3-class:** 79.6% vs 78.9%, +0.7pp at 2× params.\n\n**Table 12 - Layer placement:** V→early, S→mid, P→late pattern confirmed.\n\n**Correction Memory:** +1.2pp, p=0.08, borderline. Treated as optional.\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (imagined experiments from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper was designed with 13 experiments in total. The paper covers all major ones: expert training (plan_002), Meta-Brain assembly (plan_003), oracle ablation (plan_004), ablation ladder (plan_005), FTM comparison (plan_006), parameter efficiency (plan_007), correction memory (plan_008), router architecture (plan_009), 6-class vs 3-class (plan_010), cross-backbone SmolVLA (plan_011), layer placement (plan_012), rank-48 control (plan_013), rank sweep (plan_014), clean LIBERO (plan_015). All 13 imagined experiments appear to be covered in the paper.\n\n## Your Task\nProduce a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness**: Is the method well-motivated? Is the formulation correct? Are there gaps in the method design?\n2. **Experimental Rigor**: Are baselines appropriate? Are ablations sufficient? Statistical testing? Number of seeds? Are there missing experiments or controls?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce? Hyperparameters, training details, compute requirements?\n4. **Strengths** (bullet list)\n5. **Weaknesses** (bullet list)\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n7. **Minor Issues** (if any)\n8. **Scores**:\n   - Soundness (1-4): How technically sound is the paper?\n   - Significance (1-4): How significant are the contributions?\n   - Relevance to Robot Learning (1-5): How relevant is this to the CoRL community?\n   - Overall Score (1-10): Using CoRL scale\n   - Confidence (1-5): How confident are you in your assessment?\n\nBe critical but fair. Look for both strengths AND weaknesses. Think about what a rigorous CoRL reviewer would flag. Consider: simulation-only evaluation, closed-set assumption, the specific benchmark (LIBERO-Plus only), the VLA-GSE comparison being cross-backbone, whether the Phase 0 finding is truly novel, whether the 3-class taxonomy is justified vs. being a design choice, etc.\n\nOutput your full review in structured markdown format.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":64399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d09a97eb-2874-493a-b7bd-2546bcb68a45","uuid":"efac7dbe-6977-4e73-8af4-f22e02ecd4c0"}
